{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'for f in migrate-chartjs migrate-recharts stability; do echo $f; nl -ba apps/docs/pages/$f.md; done'","aggregated_output":"migrate-chartjs\n     1\t# Migrating from Chart.js\n     2\t\n     3\tAfter this page you can translate a Chart.js configuration into Axylo for the three everyday tasks below, map Chart.js concepts to Axylo's, and know what Axylo deliberately does differently or does not have.\n     4\t\n     5\tThe Chart.js code on this page is quoted, not retyped, from the configurations used in this project's comparison of ten charting libraries (`research/harness/src/libs/chartjs.js`). They were written against **Chart.js 4.6.1** with **chartjs-adapter-date-fns 3.0.0** and **date-fns 4.4.0**, and each is the least configuration that library needed for the task; comments mark what was required beyond the data. The Axylo versions run live on this page, on the same data.\n     6\t\n     7\t## A multi-series time line\n     8\t\n     9\tChart.js takes parallel arrays (`labels` and one `data` array per dataset), needs a date adapter before a time axis works, and needs `maintainAspectRatio: false` to fill a container of fixed height.\n    10\t\n    11\t[source: Chart.js, task \"trend\"](../../../research/harness/src/libs/chartjs.js#L1-L16)\n    12\t\n    13\tIn Axylo the same table is rows and field names. The fixture's x values are epoch milliseconds of UTC midnights, which are calendar days: `type: 'date'` reads them that way, so each value shows on its own day in every time zone. Chart.js shows the same values as local instants, which west of UTC puts every point on the day before. The gap in \"Referral\" (seven `null`s) is a gap in both.\n    14\t\n    15\t[example: migrate-trend](../examples/migrate-trend.ts)\n    16\t\n    17\t## A bar chart with a target line\n    18\t\n    19\tChart.js has no reference line of its own. The usual ways are the separate `chartjs-plugin-annotation` package, or a second dataset of `type: 'line'` repeating the target. The comparison's configuration has neither, so only its bars are quoted here:\n    20\t\n    21\t[source: Chart.js, task \"bars\"](../../../research/harness/src/libs/chartjs.js#L18-L25)\n    22\t\n    23\tIn Axylo the target is one option, `reference`, and it is labelled, included in the value axis, and listed in the chart's summary and table caption. Both libraries start these bars at zero; in Axylo a bar or area axis cannot be made to start elsewhere. The long label \"Customer Success & Onboarding\" is fitted by Axylo's remedies (wrapping, then rotating, then truncating with the full text in the tooltip and table), where Chart.js rotates all labels.\n    24\t\n    25\t[example: migrate-target](../examples/migrate-target.ts)\n    26\t\n    27\t## A live-updating series\n    28\t\n    29\tChart.js updates by mutating its arrays and calling `update()`. The comparison's stream task pushes one point and drops the oldest:\n    30\t\n    31\t[source: Chart.js, tasks \"scale\" and \"stream\"](../../../research/harness/src/libs/chartjs.js#L45-L62)\n    32\t\n    33\tIn Axylo, `append` adds rows and `keep` bounds the window. A Pause control appears for the reader, the view follows the newest data while it is zoomed to the latest edge, and arriving data is not announced to screen readers.\n    34\t\n    35\t[example: migrate-stream](../examples/migrate-stream.ts)\n    36\t\n    37\tThe comparison also has a tuned Chart.js configuration for large data (`chartjs-tuned.js`: no parsing, the decimation plugin, no animation, no point markers). Axylo has no equivalent options: typed columns and the simplified drawing of dense lines are the defaults.\n    38\t\n    39\t## Concepts side by side\n    40\t\n    41\t| Chart.js | Axylo |\n    42\t|---|---|\n    43\t| `new Chart(canvas, { type: 'line', … })` | `line(target, options)`: one function per chart type; `target` is any element or a selector, not a canvas. |\n    44\t| `data.labels` and `datasets[].data` | `data` as rows, wide rows or typed columns, and field names: `x`, `y`, `series`. See [Your data](data.md). |\n    45\t| `datasets[].label` | The `series` field's values, or `label` on each `y` field. |\n    46\t| `options.plugins.title` | `title` (also the accessible name). |\n    47\t| `scales.x.type: 'time'` and a date adapter | Nothing for date strings; `type: 'time'` for epoch milliseconds, `type: 'date'` for calendar days. No adapter. |\n    48\t| `scales.y.title` | `label` and `unit` on the `y` field. |\n    49\t| `maintainAspectRatio`, `responsive`, canvas size | Nothing: the chart takes its container's size. |\n    50\t| `scales.y.beginAtZero` | Bars and areas always start at zero; lines fit the data. |\n    51\t| `spanGaps` | No equivalent: gaps are never bridged. `missing: 'zero'` for counts. |\n    52\t| `backgroundColor`, `borderColor` | The default palette, CSS custom properties, or `colors` by series name. See [Theming](theming.md). |\n    53\t| `plugins.legend.position` | `legend: 'top' \\| 'right' \\| 'bottom' \\| false`. |\n    54\t| `plugins.tooltip` (`mode`, `intersect`) | On by default, nearest x wherever the pointer is; `tooltip: false` turns it off. |\n    55\t| `chartjs-plugin-annotation` | `reference: [{ y, label }]` or `{ x: [from, to], label }`. |\n    56\t| Mutate `chart.data`, then `chart.update()` | `chart.update(patch)` for options and data, `chart.append(rows, { keep })` for new rows. |\n    57\t| `onClick`, `onHover` | `chart.on('select', …)`, `chart.on('hover', …)`. |\n    58\t| `animation` | No option: the first render is never animated. |\n    59\t| `parsing: false`, decimation | No options: typed columns and simplified drawing are the defaults. |\n    60\t| `chart.destroy()` | `chart.destroy()`. |\n    61\t\n    62\t## What is deliberately different\n    63\t\n    64\t- **Accessible without work.** A Chart.js chart is a canvas, and making it accessible is left to you. An Axylo chart has a name, a summary, keyboard access and a table view, with no option.\n    65\t- **Bad data is reported.** Chart.js plots `'40'` among numbers as 40 and says nothing. Axylo leaves it out, tells the reader, and prints a diagnostic with the field and row ([AX106](diagnostics.md#ax106)).\n    66\t- **Time zones are named.** Instants are shown in a zone that the tooltip heading and the summary name, and calendar dates are not shifted.\n    67\t- **Fewer chart types.** Line, area, bar, scatter, donut and the compact variant. No radar, polar area, bubble or mixed charts in 1.0.\n    68\t- **Less to configure.** No plugin API, no per-point styles, no custom tooltip renderer, no animation settings, no log scale or second y axis in 1.0.\n    69\t- **Your data is not watched.** Changing an array in place is not seen; call `update` or `append`. Typed columns are borrowed and must not be changed in place.\nmigrate-recharts\n     1\t# Migrating from Recharts\n     2\t\n     3\tAfter this page you can translate a Recharts chart into an `@axylo/react` component for the three everyday tasks below, map Recharts concepts to Axylo's, and know what Axylo deliberately does differently or does not have.\n     4\t\n     5\tThe Recharts code on this page is quoted, not retyped, from the configurations used in this project's comparison of ten charting libraries (`research/harness/src/libs/recharts.jsx`). They were written against **Recharts 3.11.0** with **React 19.3.1**, and each is the least configuration that library needed for the task. Recharts has no default palette and no title component, so the comparison used the colours of Recharts' own examples. The `mount` helper renders the element into the harness's container. The Axylo versions run live on this page, on the same data.\n     6\t\n     7\t## A multi-series time line\n     8\t\n     9\tRecharts takes one row object per x with one key per series, one `<Line>` per series with its colour, and a tick formatter, because a numeric time axis prints raw epoch numbers without one.\n    10\t\n    11\t[source: Recharts, task \"trend\"](../../../research/harness/src/libs/recharts.jsx#L1-L29)\n    12\t\n    13\tIn Axylo one component holds the whole chart. Long rows with a `series` field replace one `<Line>` per series; wide rows would work too, with `y` as a list. The palette, the title, the axis titles, the date formatting, the legend and the tooltip need no code. `type: 'date'` reads the fixture's UTC-midnight milliseconds as calendar days.\n    14\t\n    15\t[example: recharts-trend](../examples/recharts-trend.tsx)\n    16\t\n    17\t## A bar chart with a target line\n    18\t\n    19\tRecharts draws a target with its `ReferenceLine` component; the comparison's configuration did not use it, so only its bars are quoted here:\n    20\t\n    21\t[source: Recharts, task \"bars\"](../../../research/harness/src/libs/recharts.jsx#L31-L46)\n    22\t\n    23\tIn Axylo the target is the `reference` prop, labelled, included in the value axis and listed in the summary and table caption. The long label is fitted instead of dropped (in the comparison, Recharts removed that label and left a bar with no name), and the chart is titled.\n    24\t\n    25\t[example: recharts-target](../examples/recharts-target.tsx)\n    26\t\n    27\t## A live-updating series\n    28\t\n    29\tThe comparison's Recharts stream re-renders with a new array for every point:\n    30\t\n    31\t[source: Recharts, tasks \"scale\" and \"stream\"](../../../research/harness/src/libs/recharts.jsx#L81-L93)\n    32\t\n    33\tWith `@axylo/react` the first rows are state, created once, and new points go through the handle with `append`, so earlier rows are not read again. The reader gets a Pause control.\n    34\t\n    35\t[example: recharts-stream](../examples/recharts-stream.tsx)\n    36\t\n    37\tRe-rendering with a new `data` array works too, and is the right thing when the whole data changes; it is the slower path for a stream.\n    38\t\n    39\t## Concepts side by side\n    40\t\n    41\t| Recharts | `@axylo/react` |\n    42\t|---|---|\n    43\t| `<LineChart data>` with `<XAxis>`, `<YAxis>`, `<CartesianGrid>`, `<Tooltip>`, `<Legend>` and one `<Line>` per series | One `<Line data x y series />`. Axes, grid, tooltip and legend are on by default. |\n    44\t| `<ResponsiveContainer>` | Nothing: the chart takes its container's size. |\n    45\t| `dataKey` per series | Long rows with `series`, or `y={['direct', 'organic']}` for wide rows. |\n    46\t| `stroke`, `fill`, `<Cell fill>` | The default palette, CSS custom properties, or `colors` by series name. See [Theming](theming.md). |\n    47\t| `<XAxis type=\"number\" scale=\"time\" tickFormatter>` | Nothing for date strings; `type: 'time'` or `type: 'date'` on `x` for numbers. Dates and numbers are formatted for the page's locale. |\n    48\t| `<YAxis label>` | `label` and `unit` on the `y` field. |\n    49\t| No title component | `title`, which is also the accessible name. |\n    50\t| `<ReferenceLine y>`, `<ReferenceArea>` | `reference={[{ y, label }]}`, or `{ x: [from, to], label }`. |\n    51\t| `<Bar>` with `stackId` | `layout=\"stacked\"` on `<Bar>`; `stacked` on `<Area>`. |\n    52\t| `layout=\"vertical\"` on `<BarChart>` | `horizontal` on `<Bar>`. |\n    53\t| `<Pie innerRadius>` | `<Donut label value />`. |\n    54\t| `isAnimationActive={false}` | Nothing: the first render is never animated. |\n    55\t| `dot={false}` | Nothing: markers appear only when points are sparse. |\n    56\t| `onClick`, `onMouseMove` on the chart | `onSelect`, `onHover`. |\n    57\t| Re-render with a new array to stream | `ref` and `chart.append(rows, { keep })`. |\n    58\t\n    59\t## What is deliberately different\n    60\t\n    61\t- **One component, one options object.** The same options work outside React with `line()`, so a chart can move between a React page and any other page unchanged.\n    62\t- **Defaults that are finished.** A palette that works in light and dark, a title, labels that fit, formatted numbers and dates, all without code.\n    63\t- **Accessible by default, differently.** Recharts' keyboard navigation (on by default in the version tested) uses `role=\"application\"`. Axylo's plot is one native range control with a text value, plus a table view; see [Accessibility](accessibility.md).\n    64\t- **Bad data is reported.** A string among numbers is left out and reported with its row ([AX106](diagnostics.md#ax106)), where Recharts plots `'40'` as 40.\n    65\t- **No composition API.** No custom shapes, custom tooltip content, label render props or `syncId` for linked charts in 1.0. A chart is configured through options, not assembled from components.\n    66\t- **Fewer chart types.** Line, area, bar, scatter, donut and the compact variant. No radar, radial bar, treemap, funnel or composed charts in 1.0.\nstability\n     1\t# Stability and releases\n     2\t\n     3\tAfter this page you know what Axylo promises between releases, which browsers and tools it supports, under what licence it ships, and what is not in 1.0.\n     4\t\n     5\t## Status\n     6\t\n     7\tThis documentation describes Axylo 1.0, which has not been released. The library in this repository is a pre-release (package version 0.0.0) and has not been published to npm. Until 1.0 is tagged, anything may change.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Versions\n    10\t\n    11\tAxylo follows semantic versioning:\n    12\t\n    13\t| Release | May contain |\n    14\t|---|---|\n    15\t| Patch (1.0.1) | Fixes that do not change documented behaviour, except to make it match the documentation. |\n    16\t| Minor (1.1.0) | New options, chart features and diagnostics, and deprecations. Nothing documented stops working. |\n    17\t| Major (2.0.0) | Removals and other breaking changes, at most one major version a year. |\n    18\t\n    19\t**Deprecation.** A deprecated API keeps working for at least one minor release and at least six months, and its documentation says what to use instead. The documented examples of the previous release must still compile and run against each release candidate.\n    20\t\n    21\t**What the promise covers.** The functions and types exported by `axylo` and `@axylo/react` (the declarations in `packages/axylo/src/public.ts`), the diagnostic codes and their levels, the CSS custom properties documented on [Theming](theming.md), and the keys of `messages`. Match diagnostics on `code`; messages are written for people.\n    22\t\n    23\t**What it does not cover.** The chart's internal DOM structure and class names, the custom properties listed as internal, the roles the plot uses to talk to assistive technology (chosen without screen-reader rehearsal, and changeable in a minor release if rehearsal shows a better pattern), and the exact pixels of the drawing.\n    24\t\n    25\t## Supported environments\n    26\t\n    27\t| Dimension | 1.0 |\n    28\t|---|---|\n    29\t| Browsers | The current and previous major versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari, on macOS and iOS. |\n    30\t| TypeScript | 5.4 and later. Plain JavaScript is fully supported; types are an aid, not a requirement. |\n    31\t| React | 18 and 19, through `@axylo/react`. |\n    32\t| Node | Importing `axylo` touches no DOM, and `validate()` runs there. Charts themselves need a browser. |\n    33\t| Text direction | Left-to-right pages. Right-to-left text renders, but the layout is not mirrored. |\n    34\t| Built-in text | English, replaceable through `messages`. |\n    35\t\n    36\tVerified so far: Chrome on Linux desktop only. Firefox, Safari, Edge, Windows, macOS and phones have not been tested yet; see [Accessibility](accessibility.md#limits).\n    37\t\n    38\t## Licence\n    39\t\n    40\tMIT, for everything: zoom, accessibility and every chart type included. There is no commercial edition and no feature behind a licence key. The library has no runtime dependencies; third-party notices, if any, are checked at each release.\n    41\t\n    42\t## What is not in 1.0\n    43\t\n    44\tNot planned for 1.0, with the reason it can wait:\n    45\t\n    46\t| Not in 1.0 | Why it can wait |\n    47\t|---|---|\n    48\t| More chart types (histogram first, then heatmap, box plot, candlestick, radar, treemap, sankey, gauge, maps) | Each must pass the same acceptance criteria as the five types in 1.0. |\n    49\t| Log and other non-linear scales | They need their own rules for zero and negative values. |\n    50\t| A second y axis | Often misleading; it needs a design that keeps the zero baseline honest. |\n    51\t| Annotations beyond reference lines and bands | Placing free text interacts with label fitting. |\n    52\t| Linked charts (shared cursor, brush) | Needs a small coordination API. |\n    53\t| Export to PNG, SVG or CSV, and print styling | CSV from the table view comes first. |\n    54\t| Server-side rendering to SVG | The drawing model makes it possible later. |\n    55\t| Right-to-left layout mirroring | Stated as a limit in 1.0. |\n    56\t| Quarters and ISO weeks as calendar periods | Treat them as ordered categories in 1.0. |\n    57\t| Nested field paths (`'user.country'`) | Flatten rows before passing them. |\n    58\t| Vue, Svelte and Angular adapters, a custom element | Thin wrappers over the same handle. |\n    59\t| A plugin or custom-mark API | Waits until two real uses show its shape. |\n    60\t| Translations of built-in text | `messages` makes them possible; only English ships. |\n    61\t| Workers, WebGL or WebGPU | Decided from measurements. |\n    62\t\n    63\tNot the audience for 1.0: analysts exploring data in notebooks, designers building bespoke graphics, and teams that need maps, financial charts or network diagrams.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'for f in apps/docs/lib/{markdown,site,examples}.mjs apps/docs/build.mjs; do echo $f; nl -ba \"$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'for f in apps/docs/lib/{markdown,site,examples}.mjs apps/docs/build.mjs; do echo $f; nl -ba \"$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"apps/docs/lib/markdown.mjs\n     1\t/**\n     2\t * The Markdown subset the documentation pages use, and nothing more: ATX headings (# to ####), paragraphs,\n     3\t * fenced code blocks, pipe tables, flat bulleted and numbered lists, block quotes, whole-line HTML comments\n     4\t * (dropped), and the inline forms `code`, **strong**, *emphasis*, [links](url) and backslash escapes.\n     5\t *\n     6\t * Raw HTML is never passed through: every character of text is escaped, so a page cannot inject markup\n     7\t * (and neither can data quoted into a page). A line that is only a link whose text starts with `example:`,\n     8\t * `source:` or `table:` is a directive; the caller decides what it becomes.\n     9\t */\n    10\t\n    11\tconst ESCAPES = { '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '\"': '&quot;', \"'\": '&#39;' };\n    12\t\n    13\t/** Escapes text for HTML element content and quoted attribute values. */\n    14\texport function escapeHtml(text) {\n    15\t  return String(text).replace(/[&<>\"']/g, c => ESCAPES[c]);\n    16\t}\n    17\t\n    18\t/**\n    19\t * A heading's id, made the way GitHub makes it, so that a link to `data.md#three-kinds-of-time` works on a\n    20\t * code host and on the site alike: lower case, punctuation dropped, each space a hyphen.\n    21\t */\n    22\texport function slug(text) {\n    23\t  return plainText(text).trim().toLowerCase().replace(/[^\\p{L}\\p{N}\\s_-]/gu, '').replace(/\\s/g, '-') || 'section';\n    24\t}\n    25\t\n    26\t/** The text a reader sees in inline Markdown: markers and link targets removed. */\n    27\texport function plainText(text) {\n    28\t  return text\n    29\t    .replace(/\\\\([\\\\`*_[\\]()|#<>!-])/g, '$1')\n    30\t    .replace(/`([^`]*)`/g, '$1')\n    31\t    .replace(/\\[([^\\]]*)\\]\\([^)]*\\)/g, '$1')\n    32\t    .replace(/\\*\\*([^*]+)\\*\\*/g, '$1')\n    33\t    .replace(/\\*([^*]+)\\*/g, '$1');\n    34\t}\n    35\t\n    36\tconst DIRECTIVE = /^\\[(example|source|table):\\s*([^\\]]+)\\]\\(([^)\\s]+)\\)$/;\n    37\tconst FENCE = /^(`{3,})\\s*([\\w-]*)\\s*$/;\n    38\tconst HEADING = /^(#{1,4})\\s+(.+?)\\s*#*\\s*$/;\n    39\tconst BULLET = /^[-*]\\s+(.*)$/;\n    40\tconst NUMBERED = /^(\\d+)\\.\\s+(.*)$/;\n    41\tconst TABLE_RULE = /^\\|?\\s*:?-{3,}:?\\s*(\\|\\s*:?-{3,}:?\\s*)*\\|?\\s*$/;\n    42\tconst COMMENT = /^<!--.*-->$/;\n    43\t\n    44\t/**\n    45\t * Converts `source` to HTML.\n    46\t * - `link(url)` rewrites a link target (for example `data.md#gaps` to `data.html#gaps`).\n    47\t * - `directive({ kind, name, target })` returns the HTML for a directive line.\n    48\t * - `headings` receives each heading as { level, text, id } in order.\n    49\t */\n    50\texport function markdownToHtml(source, { link = url => url, directive, headings = [] } = {}) {\n    51\t  const lines = source.replace(/\\r\\n?/g, '\\n').split('\\n');\n    52\t  const used = new Map();\n    53\t  const out = [];\n    54\t  const inline = text => renderInline(text, link);\n    55\t  // Each table's scroll region is named after the heading it sits under, so that no two share a name.\n    56\t  let section = null;\n    57\t  const tableNames = new Map();\n    58\t  const tableName = () => {\n    59\t    const n = (tableNames.get(section) ?? 0) + 1;\n    60\t    tableNames.set(section, n);\n    61\t    const table = n === 1 ? 'Table' : `Table ${n}`;\n    62\t    return section === null ? table : `${table}: ${section}`;\n    63\t  };\n    64\t\n    65\t  let i = 0;\n    66\t  while (i < lines.length) {\n    67\t    const line = lines[i];\n    68\t    if (line.trim() === '' || COMMENT.test(line.trim())) { i++; continue; }\n    69\t\n    70\t    const fence = FENCE.exec(line);\n    71\t    if (fence) {\n    72\t      const body = [];\n    73\t      i++;\n    74\t      while (i < lines.length && !lines[i].startsWith(fence[1])) body.push(lines[i++]);\n    75\t      if (i < lines.length) i++;\n    76\t      out.push(codeBlock(body.join('\\n'), fence[2]));\n    77\t      continue;\n    78\t    }\n    79\t\n    80\t    const heading = HEADING.exec(line);\n    81\t    if (heading) {\n    82\t      const level = heading[1].length;\n    83\t      const base = slug(heading[2]);\n    84\t      const n = (used.get(base) ?? 0) + 1;\n    85\t      used.set(base, n);\n    86\t      const id = n === 1 ? base : `${base}-${n}`;\n    87\t      headings.push({ level, text: plainText(heading[2]), id });\n    88\t      section = plainText(heading[2]);\n    89\t      out.push(`<h${level} id=\"${escapeHtml(id)}\">${inline(heading[2])}</h${level}>`);\n    90\t      i++;\n    91\t      continue;\n    92\t    }\n    93\t\n    94\t    if (line.startsWith('|') && i + 1 < lines.length && TABLE_RULE.test(lines[i + 1])) {\n    95\t      const rows = [];\n    96\t      const align = splitRow(lines[i + 1]).map(cell => cell.endsWith(':') ? (cell.startsWith(':') ? 'center' : 'right') : null);\n    97\t      const header = splitRow(line);\n    98\t      i += 2;\n    99\t      while (i < lines.length && lines[i].startsWith('|')) rows.push(splitRow(lines[i++]));\n   100\t      out.push(table(header, rows, align, inline, tableName()));\n   101\t      continue;\n   102\t    }\n   103\t\n   104\t    if (line.startsWith('>')) {\n   105\t      const body = [];\n   106\t      while (i < lines.length && lines[i].startsWith('>')) body.push(lines[i++].replace(/^>\\s?/, ''));\n   107\t      out.push(`<blockquote>${markdownToHtml(body.join('\\n'), { link, directive, headings: [] })}</blockquote>`);\n   108\t      continue;\n   109\t    }\n   110\t\n   111\t    const bullet = BULLET.exec(line);\n   112\t    const numbered = NUMBERED.exec(line);\n   113\t    if (bullet || numbered) {\n   114\t      const ordered = !bullet;\n   115\t      const marker = ordered ? NUMBERED : BULLET;\n   116\t      const items = [];\n   117\t      const start = ordered ? Number(numbered[1]) : 1;\n   118\t      while (i < lines.length) {\n   119\t        const m = marker.exec(lines[i]);\n   120\t        if (m) { items.push(ordered ? m[2] : m[1]); i++; continue; }\n   121\t        // A continuation line is indented; a blank line or anything else ends the list.\n   122\t        if (/^\\s{2,}\\S/.test(lines[i]) && items.length) { items[items.length - 1] += ' ' + lines[i].trim(); i++; continue; }\n   123\t        break;\n   124\t      }\n   125\t      const tag = ordered ? 'ol' : 'ul';\n   126\t      const startAttr = ordered && start !== 1 ? ` start=\"${start}\"` : '';\n   127\t      out.push(`<${tag}${startAttr}>${items.map(item => `<li>${inline(item)}</li>`).join('')}</${tag}>`);\n   128\t      continue;\n   129\t    }\n   130\t\n   131\t    const paragraph = [];\n   132\t    while (i < lines.length && lines[i].trim() !== '' && !startsBlock(lines, i)) paragraph.push(lines[i++].trim());\n   133\t    if (paragraph.length === 0) { paragraph.push(line.trim()); i++; }\n   134\t    const text = paragraph.join(' ');\n   135\t    const d = paragraph.length === 1 ? DIRECTIVE.exec(text) : null;\n   136\t    if (d && directive) {\n   137\t      out.push(directive({ kind: d[1], name: d[2].trim(), target: d[3] }));\n   138\t    } else {\n   139\t      out.push(`<p>${inline(text)}</p>`);\n   140\t    }\n   141\t  }\n   142\t  return out.join('\\n');\n   143\t}\n   144\t\n   145\tfunction startsBlock(lines, i) {\n   146\t  const line = lines[i];\n   147\t  return FENCE.test(line) || HEADING.test(line) || line.startsWith('>') || BULLET.test(line) || NUMBERED.test(line) ||\n   148\t    COMMENT.test(line.trim()) || (line.startsWith('|') && i + 1 < lines.length && TABLE_RULE.test(lines[i + 1]));\n   149\t}\n   150\t\n   151\t/** Splits a table row on pipes that are not escaped; `\\|` stays in the cell as a literal pipe. */\n   152\texport function splitRow(line) {\n   153\t  const cells = [];\n   154\t  let cell = '';\n   155\t  const body = line.trim().replace(/^\\|/, '').replace(/(?<!\\\\)\\|$/, '');\n   156\t  for (let i = 0; i < body.length; i++) {\n   157\t    const c = body[i];\n   158\t    if (c === '\\\\' && body[i + 1] === '|') { cell += '\\\\|'; i++; continue; }\n   159\t    if (c === '|') { cells.push(cell.trim()); cell = ''; continue; }\n   160\t    cell += c;\n   161\t  }\n   162\t  cells.push(cell.trim());\n   163\t  return cells;\n   164\t}\n   165\t\n   166\tfunction table(header, rows, align, inline, name = 'Table') {\n   167\t  const style = index => align[index] ? ` style=\"text-align: ${align[index]}\"` : '';\n   168\t  const head = header.map((cell, index) => `<th scope=\"col\"${style(index)}>${inline(cell)}</th>`).join('');\n   169\t  const body = rows.map(row => `<tr>${header.map((_, index) => `<td${style(index)}>${inline(row[index] ?? '')}</td>`).join('')}</tr>`).join('');\n   170\t  // The wrapper scrolls a wide table on a narrow screen, so the page itself never scrolls sideways.\n   171\t  return `<div class=\"table-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"${escapeHtml(name)}\"><table><thead><tr>${head}</tr></thead><tbody>${body}</tbody></table></div>`;\n   172\t}\n   173\t\n   174\texport function codeBlock(code, language = '') {\n   175\t  const cls = language ? ` class=\"language-${escapeHtml(language)}\"` : '';\n   176\t  return `<pre tabindex=\"0\"><code${cls}>${escapeHtml(code)}</code></pre>`;\n   177\t}\n   178\t\n   179\t/** Inline Markdown to HTML. Unmatched markers are kept as text. */\n   180\texport function renderInline(text, link = url => url) {\n   181\t  let out = '';\n   182\t  let i = 0;\n   183\t  while (i < text.length) {\n   184\t    const c = text[i];\n   185\t    if (c === '\\\\' && i + 1 < text.length && /[\\\\`*_[\\]()|#<>!-]/.test(text[i + 1])) {\n   186\t      out += escapeHtml(text[i + 1]);\n   187\t      i += 2;\n   188\t      continue;\n   189\t    }\n   190\t    if (c === '`') {\n   191\t      let run = 1;\n   192\t      while (text[i + run] === '`') run++;\n   193\t      const fence = '`'.repeat(run);\n   194\t      const end = text.indexOf(fence, i + run);\n   195\t      if (end !== -1) {\n   196\t        // Inside a table cell a literal pipe is written `\\|`; the backslash is not part of the code.\n   197\t        const code = text.slice(i + run, end).replace(/\\\\\\|/g, '|');\n   198\t        out += `<code>${escapeHtml(run > 1 ? code.trim() : code)}</code>`;\n   199\t        i = end + run;\n   200\t        continue;\n   201\t      }\n   202\t    }\n   203\t    if (c === '[') {\n   204\t      const close = matchBracket(text, i);\n   205\t      if (close !== -1 && text[close + 1] === '(') {\n   206\t        const end = text.indexOf(')', close + 2);\n   207\t        if (end !== -1) {\n   208\t          const label = text.slice(i + 1, close);\n   209\t          const url = text.slice(close + 2, end).trim();\n   210\t          out += `<a href=\"${escapeHtml(link(url))}\">${renderInline(label, link)}</a>`;\n   211\t          i = end + 1;\n   212\t          continue;\n   213\t        }\n   214\t      }\n   215\t    }\n   216\t    if (c === '*' && text[i + 1] === '*') {\n   217\t      const end = text.indexOf('**', i + 2);\n   218\t      if (end > i + 2) {\n   219\t        out += `<strong>${renderInline(text.slice(i + 2, end), link)}</strong>`;\n   220\t        i = end + 2;\n   221\t        continue;\n   222\t      }\n   223\t    }\n   224\t    if (c === '*' && text[i + 1] !== ' ' && text[i + 1] !== '*') {\n   225\t      const end = text.indexOf('*', i + 1);\n   226\t      if (end > i + 1 && text[end - 1] !== ' ') {\n   227\t        out += `<em>${renderInline(text.slice(i + 1, end), link)}</em>`;\n   228\t        i = end + 1;\n   229\t        continue;\n   230\t      }\n   231\t    }\n   232\t    out += escapeHtml(c);\n   233\t    i++;\n   234\t  }\n   235\t  return out;\n   236\t}\n   237\t\n   238\tfunction matchBracket(text, open) {\n   239\t  let depth = 0;\n   240\t  for (let i = open; i < text.length; i++) {\n   241\t    if (text[i] === '\\\\') { i++; continue; }\n   242\t    if (text[i] === '`') {\n   243\t      const end = text.indexOf('`', i + 1);\n   244\t      if (end !== -1) { i = end; continue; }\n   245\t    }\n   246\t    if (text[i] === '[') depth++;\n   247\t    if (text[i] === ']' && --depth === 0) return i;\n   248\t  }\n   249\t  return -1;\n   250\t}\n   251\t\n   252\t/** Words of prose in a page, for the report: code blocks, comments and table rules are not counted. */\n   253\texport function wordCount(source) {\n   254\t  let inCode = false;\n   255\t  let words = 0;\n   256\t  for (const line of source.split('\\n')) {\n   257\t    if (FENCE.test(line)) { inCode = !inCode; continue; }\n   258\t    if (inCode || COMMENT.test(line.trim()) || TABLE_RULE.test(line) || DIRECTIVE.test(line.trim())) continue;\n   259\t    words += plainText(line.replace(/\\|/g, ' ')).split(/\\s+/).filter(w => /[\\p{L}\\p{N}]/u.test(w)).length;\n   260\t  }\n   261\t  return words;\n   262\t}\napps/docs/lib/site.mjs\n     1\t/**\n     2\t * Builds the documentation site into apps/docs/dist from the Markdown pages, the runnable examples, the\n     3\t * diagnostics data file and the library's built files (packages/axylo/dist, packages/react/dist).\n     4\t *\n     5\t * Every example runs live in its own page (dist/examples/<name>.html) against the built library, loaded\n     6\t * through an import map, and is embedded in the documentation page beside its source. Each example page is\n     7\t * its own document so that its ids, its console and Axylo's once-per-page printing of diagnostics belong to\n     8\t * that example alone; the browser test opens the same pages.\n     9\t */\n    10\timport fs from 'node:fs';\n    11\timport path from 'node:path';\n    12\timport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\n    13\timport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\n    14\timport { build } from 'esbuild';\n    15\timport { escapeHtml, markdownToHtml, codeBlock, renderInline, wordCount, slug } from './markdown.mjs';\n    16\timport { cacheDir, docsRoot, listExamples, repoRoot } from './examples.mjs';\n    17\timport { nav, pages } from '../data/nav.mjs';\n    18\t\n    19\tconst libDist = path.join(repoRoot, 'packages/axylo/dist');\n    20\tconst reactDist = path.join(repoRoot, 'packages/react/dist');\n    21\tconst pagesDir = path.join(docsRoot, 'pages');\n    22\tconst siteDir = path.join(docsRoot, 'site');\n    23\t\n    24\tconst REQUIRED = [\n    25\t  [libDist, ['axylo.js', 'axylo.dev.js', 'axylo.iife.js', 'axylo.iife.min.js', 'axylo.css', 'index.d.ts']],\n    26\t  [reactDist, ['index.js', 'index.dev.js', 'index.d.ts']],\n    27\t];\n    28\t\n    29\t/** Fails with the command to run when the library has not been built. */\n    30\texport function checkLibraryBuilt() {\n    31\t  const missing = REQUIRED.flatMap(([dir, files]) => files.map(f => path.join(dir, f)).filter(f => !fs.existsSync(f)));\n    32\t  if (missing.length) {\n    33\t    throw new Error(`The library is not built (missing ${missing.map(f => path.relative(repoRoot, f)).join(', ')}). Run \\`npm run build\\` first.`);\n    34\t  }\n    35\t}\n    36\t\n    37\t/** Bundles a TypeScript source of the library and imports it, to read data the built bundle does not export. */\n    38\texport async function importSource(relative) {\n    39\t  const result = await build({\n    40\t    entryPoints: [path.join(repoRoot, relative)], bundle: true, format: 'esm', write: false, platform: 'neutral',\n    41\t    define: { __DEV__: 'true' }, logLevel: 'silent',\n    42\t  });\n    43\t  return import('data:text/javascript;base64,' + Buffer.from(result.outputFiles[0].contents).toString('base64'));\n    44\t}\n    45\t\n    46\t/**\n    47\t * The default token values of the built stylesheet, per scheme: `--axylo-default-axis` → `#5f6470`. Read from\n    48\t * dist/axylo.css, so the site shows what ships.\n    49\t */\n    50\texport function readThemeDefaults(css = fs.readFileSync(path.join(libDist, 'axylo.css'), 'utf8')) {\n    51\t  const block = selector => {\n    52\t    const at = css.indexOf(selector + ' {');\n    53\t    if (at === -1) throw new Error(`axylo.css has no \"${selector}\" block`);\n    54\t    const body = css.slice(at + selector.length + 2, css.indexOf('}', at));\n    55\t    return Object.fromEntries([...body.matchAll(/(--axylo-default-[\\w-]+):\\s*([^;]+);/g)].map(m => [m[1], m[2].trim()]));\n    56\t  };\n    57\t  return { light: block('.axylo'), dark: block('.axylo[data-axylo-scheme=\"dark\"]') };\n    58\t}\n    59\t\n    60\tconst HEX = /^#[0-9a-f]{3,8}$/i;\n    61\t\n    62\texport async function buildSite({ outDir = path.join(docsRoot, 'dist'), log = () => {} } = {}) {\n    63\t  checkLibraryBuilt();\n    64\t  const warnings = [];\n    65\t  fs.rmSync(outDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    66\t  for (const dir of ['assets/vendor', 'examples', 'diagnostics']) fs.mkdirSync(path.join(outDir, dir), { recursive: true });\n    67\t\n    68\t  const theme = readThemeDefaults();\n    69\t  writeAssets(outDir, theme);\n    70\t  await buildVendor(outDir);\n    71\t  const examples = await buildExamples(outDir);\n    72\t  const { diagnostics } = await import(pathToFileURL(path.join(docsRoot, 'data/diagnostics.mjs')).href + `?t=${Date.now()}`);\n    73\t  const { tokens, internalTokens } = await import(pathToFileURL(path.join(docsRoot, 'data/tokens.mjs')).href + `?t=${Date.now()}`);\n    74\t  const messages = (await importSource('packages/axylo/src/messages/index.ts')).defaultMessages;\n    75\t  const seen = await diagnosticOutput(diagnostics);\n    76\t  const version = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(repoRoot, 'packages/axylo/package.json'), 'utf8')).version;\n    77\t\n    78\t  const context = { outDir, examples, diagnostics, seen, tokens, internalTokens, messages, theme, warnings, version };\n    79\t  const report = [];\n    80\t  for (const [index, entry] of pages.entries()) {\n    81\t    const file = path.join(pagesDir, `${entry.page}.md`);\n    82\t    const source = fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n    83\t    const html = renderPage(entry, source, index, context);\n    84\t    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(outDir, `${entry.page}.html`), html);\n    85\t    report.push({ page: entry.page, words: wordCount(source) });\n    86\t  }\n    87\t  for (const d of diagnostics) {\n    88\t    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(outDir, 'diagnostics', `${d.code}.html`), renderDiagnosticPage(d, context));\n    89\t  }\n    90\t  const broken = checkLinks(outDir);\n    91\t  if (broken.length) throw new Error('Broken links:\\n' + broken.join('\\n'));\n    92\t  for (const w of warnings) log('warning: ' + w);\n    93\t  return { pages: report, examples, warnings, diagnostics: diagnostics.length };\n    94\t}\n    95\t\n    96\t// ---------- assets ----------\n    97\t\n    98\tfunction writeAssets(outDir, theme) {\n    99\t  const pick = (scheme, name) => {\n   100\t    const value = theme[scheme][`--axylo-default-${name}`];\n   101\t    if (!value || !HEX.test(value)) throw new Error(`axylo.css: no colour for --axylo-default-${name} (${scheme})`);\n   102\t    return value;\n   103\t  };\n   104\t  // The site's surfaces use the chart's own default tokens, so the pages and the charts match.\n   105\t  const vars = scheme => ['background', 'axis', 'grid', 'muted', 'focus', 'reference']\n   106\t    .map(name => `  --site-${name}: ${pick(scheme, name)};`).join('\\n');\n   107\t  const tokens = `/* Generated from packages/axylo/dist/axylo.css by apps/docs/lib/site.mjs. */\n   108\t:root {\n   109\t${vars('light')}\n   110\t}\n   111\t@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n   112\t  :root {\n   113\t${vars('dark')}\n   114\t  }\n   115\t}\n   116\t`;\n   117\t  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(outDir, 'assets/site.css'), tokens + fs.readFileSync(path.join(siteDir, 'site.css'), 'utf8'));\n   118\t  for (const file of ['page.js', 'frame.js']) fs.copyFileSync(path.join(siteDir, file), path.join(outDir, 'assets', file));\n   119\t  // The development flavour, so example pages print hints as an application in development would.\n   120\t  fs.copyFileSync(path.join(libDist, 'axylo.dev.js'), path.join(outDir, 'assets/axylo.js'));\n   121\t  fs.copyFileSync(path.join(reactDist, 'index.dev.js'), path.join(outDir, 'assets/axylo-react.js'));\n   122\t  // Next to the example pages, so the script-tag example reads `<script src=\"axylo.iife.js\">` as a reader would write it.\n   123\t  fs.copyFileSync(path.join(libDist, 'axylo.iife.js'), path.join(outDir, 'examples/axylo.iife.js'));\n   124\t  fs.copyFileSync(path.join(libDist, 'axylo.css'), path.join(outDir, 'examples/axylo.css'));\n   125\t}\n   126\t\n   127\t/**\n   128\t * React and React DOM as ES modules for the import map. Both packages are CommonJS, so each entry is a small\n   129\t * module that re-exports the names the package has, read from the package itself.\n   130\t */\n   131\tasync function buildVendor(outDir) {\n   132\t  const require = createRequire(path.join(repoRoot, 'package.json'));\n   133\t  const dir = path.join(cacheDir, 'vendor');\n   134\t  fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\n   135\t  const entries = { react: 'react', 'jsx-runtime': 'react/jsx-runtime', 'react-dom-client': 'react-dom/client' };\n   136\t  const entryPoints = {};\n   137\t  for (const [out, specifier] of Object.entries(entries)) {\n   138\t    const names = Object.keys(require(specifier)).filter(n => /^[A-Za-z_$][\\w$]*$/.test(n) && n !== 'default');\n   139\t    const file = path.join(dir, `${out}.mjs`);\n   140\t    fs.writeFileSync(file, `import m from '${specifier}';\\nexport default m;\\n${names.map(n => `export const ${n} = m.${n};`).join('\\n')}\\n`);\n   141\t    entryPoints[out] = file;\n   142\t  }\n   143\t  await build({\n   144\t    entryPoints, bundle: true, format: 'esm', splitting: true, outdir: path.join(outDir, 'assets/vendor'), target: 'es2022',\n   145\t    define: { 'process.env.NODE_ENV': '\"development\"' }, logLevel: 'warning', nodePaths: [path.join(repoRoot, 'node_modules')],\n   146\t    absWorkingDir: repoRoot,\n   147\t  });\n   148\t}\n   149\t\n   150\t// ---------- examples ----------\n   151\t\n   152\tconst IMPORT_MAP = JSON.stringify({ imports: {\n   153\t  axylo: '../assets/axylo.js',\n   154\t  '@axylo/react': '../assets/axylo-react.js',\n   155\t  react: '../assets/vendor/react.js',\n   156\t  'react/jsx-runtime': '../assets/vendor/jsx-runtime.js',\n   157\t  'react-dom/client': '../assets/vendor/react-dom-client.js',\n   158\t} }, null, 2);\n   159\t\n   160\tasync function buildExamples(outDir) {\n   161\t  const examples = listExamples();\n   162\t  const compiled = examples.filter(e => e.ext !== 'html');\n   163\t  if (compiled.length) {\n   164\t    await build({\n   165\t      entryPoints: compiled.map(e => path.join(docsRoot, 'examples', e.file)), bundle: true, format: 'esm', target: 'es2022',\n   166\t      outdir: path.join(outDir, 'examples'), jsx: 'automatic', logLevel: 'warning',\n   167\t      external: ['axylo', '@axylo/react', 'react', 'react/jsx-runtime', 'react-dom', 'react-dom/client'],\n   168\t    });\n   169\t  }\n   170\t  const manifest = [];\n   171\t  for (const e of examples) {\n   172\t    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(outDir, 'examples', `${e.name}.html`), examplePage(e));\n   173\t    manifest.push({ name: e.name, file: e.file, ext: e.ext, raises: e.raises, noMarks: e.noMarks });\n   174\t  }\n   175\t  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(outDir, 'examples/manifest.json'), JSON.stringify(manifest, null, 2));\n   176\t  return manifest;\n   177\t}\n   178\t\n   179\tfunction examplePage(e) {\n   180\t  // An .html example's own <style> goes to the head, where it belongs; the reader sees it in the source as written.\n   181\t  const styles = e.ext === 'html' ? [...e.source.matchAll(/<style>[\\s\\S]*?<\\/style>\\n?/g)].map(m => m[0]).join('') : '';\n   182\t  const body = e.ext === 'html'\n   183\t    ? e.source.replace(/<style>[\\s\\S]*?<\\/style>\\n?/g, '')\n   184\t    : e.ext === 'tsx'\n   185\t      ? '<div id=\"root\"></div>\\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"' + e.name + '.js\"></script>'\n   186\t      : e.targets.map(id => `<div id=\"${escapeHtml(id)}\" class=\"example-target\"></div>`).join('\\n') +\n   187\t        `\\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"${e.name}.js\"></script>`;\n   188\t  return `<!doctype html>\n   189\t<html lang=\"en\">\n   190\t<head>\n   191\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n   192\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n   193\t<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">\n   194\t<title>Example: ${escapeHtml(e.name)}</title>\n   195\t<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\">\n   196\t<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/site.css\">\n   197\t<script type=\"importmap\">\n   198\t${IMPORT_MAP}\n   199\t</script>\n   200\t<script src=\"../assets/frame.js\" defer></script>\n   201\t${styles}</head>\n   202\t<body class=\"example-page\">\n   203\t${body}\n   204\t</body>\n   205\t</html>\n   206\t`;\n   207\t}\n   208\t\n   209\t// ---------- pages ----------\n   210\t\n   211\tfunction renderPage(entry, source, index, ctx) {\n   212\t  const headings = [];\n   213\t  const where = path.join(pagesDir, `${entry.page}.md`);\n   214\t  const body = markdownToHtml(source, {\n   215\t    headings,\n   216\t    link: url => pageLink(url),\n   217\t    directive: d => directive(d, where, ctx),\n   218\t  });\n   219\t  const title = headings.find(h => h.level === 1)?.text ?? entry.label;\n   220\t  const prev = pages[index - 1];\n   221\t  const next = pages[index + 1];\n   222\t  const pager = `<nav class=\"pager\" aria-label=\"Previous and next page\">${prev ? `<a rel=\"prev\" href=\"${prev.page}.html\">← ${escapeHtml(prev.label)}</a>` : '<span></span>'}${next ? `<a rel=\"next\" href=\"${next.page}.html\">${escapeHtml(next.label)} →</a>` : ''}</nav>`;\n   223\t  return layout({\n   224\t    title, body: body + pager, current: entry.page, base: '', ctx,\n   225\t    sourcePath: `apps/docs/pages/${entry.page}.md`,\n   226\t  });\n   227\t}\n   228\t\n   229\tconst PAGE_NAMES = new Set(pages.map(p => p.page));\n   230\t\n   231\t/** Rewrites a link written for the Markdown sources (readable on a code host) to its place in the site. */\n   232\texport function pageLink(url, base = '') {\n   233\t  if (/^[a-z]+:/i.test(url) || url.startsWith('#')) return url;\n   234\t  const [file, hash] = url.split('#');\n   235\t  const code = file === 'diagnostics.md' && hash && /^ax\\d{3}$/i.test(hash) ? hash.toUpperCase() : null;\n   236\t  if (code) return `${base}diagnostics/${code}.html`;\n   237\t  const name = file.endsWith('.md') && !file.includes('/') ? file.slice(0, -3) : null;\n   238\t  if (name !== null && PAGE_NAMES.has(name)) return `${base}${name}.html${hash ? '#' + hash : ''}`;\n   239\t  // A path into the repository: pages/ and dist/ sit at the same depth, so it resolves the same from both\n   240\t  // when the site is served from the repository root.\n   241\t  return base + url;\n   242\t}\n   243\t\n   244\tfunction directive({ kind, name, target }, where, ctx) {\n   245\t  if (kind === 'example') return exampleBlock(name, target, where, ctx);\n   246\t  if (kind === 'source') return sourceBlock(name, target, where, ctx);\n   247\t  if (kind === 'table') return generatedTable(name, ctx);\n   248\t  throw new Error(`Unknown directive ${kind}`);\n   249\t}\n   250\t\n   251\tfunction exampleBlock(name, target, where, ctx) {\n   252\t  const file = path.resolve(path.dirname(where), target);\n   253\t  const example = ctx.examples.find(e => path.join(docsRoot, 'examples', e.file) === file);\n   254\t  if (!example) throw new Error(`${path.relative(repoRoot, where)}: example ${target} does not exist`);\n   255\t  if (example.name !== name) throw new Error(`${path.relative(repoRoot, where)}: example link text \"${name}\" does not match ${example.file}`);\n   256\t  const source = fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n   257\t  const targets = example.ext === 'ts' ? Math.max(1, (source.match(/\\b(?:line|area|bar|scatter|donut)\\(\\s*['\"]#/g) ?? []).length) : 1;\n   258\t  const raises = example.raises.length\n   259\t    ? `<p class=\"example-note\">This example raises ${listText(example.raises.map(c => `<a href=\"diagnostics/${c}.html\">${c}</a>`))} on purpose.</p>`\n   260\t    : '';\n   261\t  const height = example.ext === 'ts' ? targets * 470 : 470;\n   262\t  return `<figure class=\"example\" id=\"example-${escapeHtml(example.name)}\">\n   263\t<div class=\"example-live\"><iframe src=\"examples/${escapeHtml(example.name)}.html\" title=\"Live example: ${escapeHtml(example.name)}\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"height: ${height}px\"></iframe></div>\n   264\t${raises}<figcaption><span>Source</span> <a href=\"../examples/${escapeHtml(example.file)}\">examples/${escapeHtml(example.file)}</a> · <a href=\"examples/${escapeHtml(example.name)}.html\">open on its own</a></figcaption>\n   265\t${codeBlock(source, example.ext)}\n   266\t</figure>`;\n   267\t}\n   268\t\n   269\t/** \"a\", \"a and b\", \"a, b and c\". */\n   270\tfunction listText(items) {\n   271\t  return items.length < 2 ? items.join('') : `${items.slice(0, -1).join(', ')} and ${items[items.length - 1]}`;\n   272\t}\n   273\t\n   274\tfunction sourceBlock(label, target, where, ctx) {\n   275\t  const [file, range] = target.split('#');\n   276\t  const absolute = path.resolve(path.dirname(where), file);\n   277\t  const shown = path.relative(repoRoot, absolute);\n   278\t  if (!fs.existsSync(absolute)) {\n   279\t    ctx.warnings.push(`${path.relative(repoRoot, where)}: ${shown} does not exist yet; the page shows a placeholder`);\n   280\t    return `<figure class=\"source source-missing\"><figcaption>${escapeHtml(label)}</figcaption><p>This snippet is quoted from <code>${escapeHtml(shown)}</code>, which did not exist when this site was built.</p></figure>`;\n   281\t  }\n   282\t  let text = fs.readFileSync(absolute, 'utf8').replace(/\\n$/, '');\n   283\t  const lines = range && /^L(\\d+)-L(\\d+)$/.exec(range);\n   284\t  if (range && !lines) throw new Error(`${path.relative(repoRoot, where)}: bad line range ${range}`);\n   285\t  if (lines) {\n   286\t    const all = text.split('\\n');\n   287\t    const [from, to] = [Number(lines[1]), Number(lines[2])];\n   288\t    if (from < 1 || to > all.length || from > to) throw new Error(`${path.relative(repoRoot, where)}: ${shown} has no lines ${from}–${to}`);\n   289\t    text = all.slice(from - 1, to).join('\\n');\n   290\t  }\n   291\t  const ext = path.extname(file).slice(1);\n   292\t  const named = label === shown || label === file ? '' : `${escapeHtml(label)} · `;\n   293\t  return `<figure class=\"source\"><figcaption>${named}<a href=\"${escapeHtml(target)}\">${escapeHtml(shown)}${lines ? `, lines ${lines[1]}–${lines[2]}` : ''}</a></figcaption>${codeBlock(text, ext)}</figure>`;\n   294\t}\n   295\t\n   296\tfunction generatedTable(name, ctx) {\n   297\t  if (name === 'diagnostic codes') return diagnosticsTable(ctx);\n   298\t  if (name === 'theme tokens') return tokensTable(ctx);\n   299\t  if (name === 'internal tokens') return internalTokensTable(ctx);\n   300\t  if (name === 'messages') return messagesTable(ctx);\n   301\t  if (name === 'palette') return paletteTable(ctx);\n   302\t  throw new Error(`Unknown generated table \"${name}\"`);\n   303\t}\n   304\t\n   305\tfunction htmlTable(head, rows, caption) {\n   306\t  const th = head.map(h => `<th scope=\"col\">${escapeHtml(h)}</th>`).join('');\n   307\t  return `<div class=\"table-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"${escapeHtml(caption)}\"><table><thead><tr>${th}</tr></thead><tbody>${rows.map(r => `<tr>${r.join('')}</tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div>`;\n   308\t}\n   309\t\n   310\tfunction diagnosticsTable(ctx) {\n   311\t  const rows = ctx.diagnostics.map(d => [\n   312\t    `<th scope=\"row\"><a href=\"diagnostics/${d.code}.html\">${d.code}</a></th>`,\n   313\t    `<td><span class=\"level level-${d.level}\">${escapeHtml(d.level)}</span></td>`,\n   314\t    `<td>${renderInline(d.condition)}</td>`,\n   315\t    `<td>${renderInline(d.drawn)}</td>`,\n   316\t  ]);\n   317\t  return htmlTable(['Code', 'Level', 'When', 'What is drawn'], rows, 'Diagnostic codes');\n   318\t}\n   319\t\n   320\tfunction swatch(value) {\n   321\t  // Only a colour read from the library's own stylesheet reaches a style attribute, and only as a hex value.\n   322\t  if (!HEX.test(value)) return `<code>${escapeHtml(value)}</code>`;\n   323\t  return `<span class=\"swatch\" style=\"background: ${value}\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><code>${escapeHtml(value)}</code>`;\n   324\t}\n   325\t\n   326\tfunction tokensTable(ctx) {\n   327\t  const rows = ctx.tokens.map(t => {\n   328\t    const cell = scheme => t.default\n   329\t      ? `<td>${swatch(ctx.theme[scheme][t.default] ?? missing(t.default, scheme))}</td>`\n   330\t      : `<td>${renderInline(t.unset)}</td>`;\n   331\t    // What it affects comes before the defaults, so a phone shows it without scrolling the table.\n   332\t    return [`<th scope=\"row\"><code>${escapeHtml(t.name)}</code></th>`, `<td class=\"wide\">${renderInline(t.affects)}</td>`, cell('light'), cell('dark')];\n   333\t  });\n   334\t  return htmlTable(['Property', 'What it affects', 'Light default', 'Dark default'], rows, 'Theme custom properties');\n   335\t}\n   336\t\n   337\tfunction missing(name, scheme) {\n   338\t  throw new Error(`axylo.css has no ${name} in the ${scheme} scheme`);\n   339\t}\n   340\t\n   341\tfunction internalTokensTable(ctx) {\n   342\t  const rows = ctx.internalTokens.map(t => [`<th scope=\"row\"><code>${escapeHtml(t.name)}</code></th>`, `<td>${renderInline(t.why)}</td>`]);\n   343\t  return htmlTable(['Property', 'Why it exists'], rows, 'Internal custom properties');\n   344\t}\n   345\t\n   346\tfunction messagesTable(ctx) {\n   347\t  const rows = Object.entries(ctx.messages).map(([key, text]) => [\n   348\t    `<th scope=\"row\"><code>${escapeHtml(key)}</code></th>`, `<td>${escapeHtml(text)}</td>`,\n   349\t  ]);\n   350\t  return htmlTable(['Key', 'Built-in English text'], rows, 'Built-in messages');\n   351\t}\n   352\t\n   353\tfunction paletteTable(ctx) {\n   354\t  const rows = [];\n   355\t  for (let slot = 1; ; slot++) {\n   356\t    const name = `--axylo-default-series-${slot}`;\n   357\t    if (!(name in ctx.theme.light)) break;\n   358\t    rows.push([`<th scope=\"row\">${slot}</th>`, `<td>${swatch(ctx.theme.light[name])}</td>`, `<td>${swatch(ctx.theme.dark[name])}</td>`]);\n   359\t  }\n   360\t  return htmlTable(['Slot', 'Light', 'Dark'], rows, 'Default palette');\n   361\t}\n   362\t\n   363\t// ---------- diagnostics ----------\n   364\t\n   365\t/**\n   366\t * What each code's minimal input prints. Inputs that run in Node go through the built library's `validate()`,\n   367\t * so the page shows the message exactly as the library writes it; the others need a browser (contrast, size,\n   368\t * labels, formatters, appends) and show the registry's message for the sample details in the data file.\n   369\t */\n   370\tasync function diagnosticOutput(diagnostics) {\n   371\t  const lib = await import(pathToFileURL(path.join(libDist, 'axylo.js')).href);\n   372\t  const registry = await importSource('packages/axylo/src/diagnostics/registry.ts');\n   373\t  const out = new Map();\n   374\t  for (const d of diagnostics) {\n   375\t    if (d.run === 'node') {\n   376\t      const found = new Function('validate', `return ${d.input}`)(lib.validate);\n   377\t      const mine = found.filter(x => x.code === d.code);\n   378\t      if (mine.length === 0) throw new Error(`${d.code}: the minimal input does not raise it (got ${found.map(x => x.code).join(', ') || 'nothing'})`);\n   379\t      out.set(d.code, mine.map(x => `[axylo ${x.code}] ${JSON.stringify(x.chart)}: ${x.message}`));\n   380\t    } else {\n   381\t      const made = registry.createDiagnostic(d.code, d.sample?.effect ?? 'none', d.sample?.details ?? {});\n   382\t      out.set(d.code, [`[axylo ${d.code}] ${JSON.stringify(d.sample?.chart ?? 'Chart title')}: ${made.message}`]);\n   383\t    }\n   384\t  }\n   385\t  return out;\n   386\t}\n   387\t\n   388\tfunction renderDiagnosticPage(d, ctx) {\n   389\t  const md = s => markdownToHtml(s, { link: url => pageLink(url, '../') });\n   390\t  const index = ctx.diagnostics.indexOf(d);\n   391\t  const prev = ctx.diagnostics[index - 1];\n   392\t  const next = ctx.diagnostics[index + 1];\n   393\t  const how = d.run === 'node'\n   394\t    ? 'Checked with <code>validate()</code> in Node when this site was built; the message above is its output.'\n   395\t    : 'This code needs a browser to arise. The browser test renders this input and checks that the code is reported; the message above is the registry text for sample details.';\n   396\t  const body = `<p class=\"crumb\"><a href=\"../diagnostics.html\">Diagnostics</a> › ${d.code}</p>\n   397\t<h1 id=\"top\">${d.code}: ${escapeHtml(d.title)}</h1>\n   398\t<p><span class=\"level level-${d.level}\">${escapeHtml(d.level)}</span> ${renderInline(levelText(d.level), url => pageLink(url, '../'))}</p>\n   399\t<h2 id=\"what-you-see\">What you see</h2>\n   400\t${md(d.see)}\n   401\t${codeBlock(ctx.seen.get(d.code).join('\\n'), 'text')}\n   402\t<h2 id=\"why\">Why</h2>\n   403\t${md(d.why)}\n   404\t<h2 id=\"how-to-fix\">How to fix it</h2>\n   405\t${md(d.fix)}\n   406\t<h2 id=\"minimal-input\">A minimal input that raises it</h2>\n   407\t${codeBlock(d.input, 'js')}\n   408\t<p class=\"small\">${how}</p>\n   409\t<nav class=\"pager\" aria-label=\"Previous and next code\">${prev ? `<a rel=\"prev\" href=\"${prev.code}.html\">← ${prev.code}</a>` : '<span></span>'}${next ? `<a rel=\"next\" href=\"${next.code}.html\">${next.code} →</a>` : ''}</nav>`;\n   410\t  return layout({ title: `${d.code}: ${d.title}`, body, current: 'diagnostics', base: '../', ctx, sourcePath: `apps/docs/data/diagnostics.mjs` });\n   411\t}\n   412\t\n   413\tfunction levelText(level) {\n   414\t  if (level === 'error') return 'The chart, or the affected series, cannot be drawn: the chart shows its error state. Printed in every build; thrown by a `strict` chart.';\n   415\t  if (level === 'warning') return 'Something is not drawn as given; when values were left out or changed, the reader sees a note. Printed in every build; thrown by a `strict` chart when it comes from a call.';\n   416\t  return 'Advice for the author. Printed in development builds only; never thrown.';\n   417\t}\n   418\t\n   419\t// ---------- layout ----------\n   420\t\n   421\tfunction layout({ title, body, current, base, ctx, sourcePath }) {\n   422\t  const links = mobile => nav.map(group => `<li><span class=\"nav-section\">${escapeHtml(group.section)}</span><ul>${group.pages.map(p =>\n   423\t    `<li><a href=\"${base}${p.page}.html\"${p.page === current ? ' aria-current=\"page\"' : ''}>${escapeHtml(p.label)}</a></li>`).join('')}</ul></li>`).join('');\n   424\t  return `<!doctype html>\n   425\t<html lang=\"en\">\n   426\t<head>\n   427\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n   428\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n   429\t<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">\n   430\t<title>${escapeHtml(title)} · Axylo</title>\n   431\t<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\">\n   432\t<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"${base}assets/site.css\">\n   433\t<script src=\"${base}assets/page.js\" defer></script>\n   434\t</head>\n   435\t<body>\n   436\t<a class=\"skip\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a>\n   437\t<header class=\"site-header\">\n   438\t<a class=\"brand\" href=\"${base}index.html\">Axylo</a><span class=\"tagline\">Documentation for 1.0</span>\n   439\t</header>\n   440\t<details class=\"nav-mobile\"><summary>Pages</summary><nav aria-label=\"Documentation\"><ul class=\"nav-list\">${links(true)}</ul></nav></details>\n   441\t<div class=\"layout\">\n   442\t<nav class=\"nav-side\" aria-label=\"Documentation\"><ul class=\"nav-list\">${links(false)}</ul></nav>\n   443\t<main id=\"main\">\n   444\t<article>\n   445\t${body}\n   446\t</article>\n   447\t<footer class=\"page-footer\"><p>Source of this page: <code>${escapeHtml(sourcePath)}</code>. The live examples run the library's built files (package version ${escapeHtml(ctx.version)}, development flavour).</p></footer>\n   448\t</main>\n   449\t</div>\n   450\t</body>\n   451\t</html>\n   452\t`;\n   453\t}\n   454\t\n   455\t// ---------- links ----------\n   456\t\n   457\t/** Every link in the built site resolves: pages and their anchors in dist, other paths in the repository. */\n   458\texport function checkLinks(outDir) {\n   459\t  const broken = [];\n   460\t  const files = [];\n   461\t  const walk = dir => {\n   462\t    for (const f of fs.readdirSync(dir)) {\n   463\t      const p = path.join(dir, f);\n   464\t      if (fs.statSync(p).isDirectory()) walk(p);\n   465\t      else if (f.endsWith('.html')) files.push(p);\n   466\t    }\n   467\t  };\n   468\t  walk(outDir);\n   469\t  const ids = new Map();\n   470\t  const idsOf = file => {\n   471\t    if (!ids.has(file)) ids.set(file, new Set([...fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8').matchAll(/\\sid=\"([^\"]+)\"/g)].map(m => m[1])));\n   472\t    return ids.get(file);\n   473\t  };\n   474\t  for (const file of files) {\n   475\t    const html = fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n   476\t    for (const m of html.matchAll(/\\s(?:href|src)=\"([^\"]+)\"/g)) {\n   477\t      const url = m[1].replace(/&amp;/g, '&');\n   478\t      if (/^[a-z]+:/i.test(url)) continue;\n   479\t      const [target, hash] = url.split('#');\n   480\t      const resolved = target === '' ? file : path.resolve(path.dirname(file), decodeURIComponent(target));\n   481\t      if (!fs.existsSync(resolved)) { broken.push(`${path.relative(outDir, file)} → ${url}`); continue; }\n   482\t      if (hash && resolved.endsWith('.html') && resolved.startsWith(outDir) && !/^L\\d+/.test(hash) && !idsOf(resolved).has(hash)) {\n   483\t        broken.push(`${path.relative(outDir, file)} → ${url} (no such anchor)`);\n   484\t      }\n   485\t    }\n   486\t  }\n   487\t  return broken;\n   488\t}\n   489\t\n   490\texport { slug };\napps/docs/lib/examples.mjs\n     1\t/**\n     2\t * Runnable examples: files in apps/docs/examples, each one a complete program a reader can copy.\n     3\t *\n     4\t * - `name.ts`: a module that imports from 'axylo' and draws into elements it names by id, as in\n     5\t *   `line('#chart', …)`. The example page creates one empty <div> per id it finds in such a call.\n     6\t * - `name.tsx`: a React module that renders into `#root`.\n     7\t * - `name.html`: markup and scripts for the body of the page, for examples that need their own markup.\n     8\t *\n     9\t * What an example promises is written in its own comments, in words the reader sees too:\n    10\t * - \"Raises AX111 on purpose\" (or \"Raises AX102, AX103 and AX106 on purpose\") lists the diagnostics it\n    11\t *   demonstrates; the browser test fails on any other code, and on a listed code that does not appear.\n    12\t * - \"Draws no marks on purpose\" marks an example whose charts show a state (loading, empty, error) instead.\n    13\t */\n    14\timport fs from 'node:fs';\n    15\timport path from 'node:path';\n    16\t\n    17\texport const docsRoot = path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, '..');\n    18\texport const repoRoot = path.resolve(docsRoot, '../..');\n    19\texport const examplesDir = path.join(docsRoot, 'examples');\n    20\t/** Scratch output that is not the site: generated type-check inputs and the vendor shims. Git-ignored. */\n    21\texport const cacheDir = path.join(docsRoot, '.cache');\n    22\t\n    23\tconst CHART_CALL = /\\b(?:line|area|bar|scatter|donut)\\(\\s*(['\"])#([\\w-]+)\\1/g;\n    24\tconst RAISES = /Raises ((?:AX\\d{3})(?:(?:, | and )AX\\d{3})*) on purpose/;\n    25\tconst NO_MARKS = /Draws no marks on purpose/;\n    26\tconst MODULE_SCRIPT = /<script type=\"module\">([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/script>/g;\n    27\tconst CLASSIC_SCRIPT = /<script>([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/script>/g;\n    28\t\n    29\texport function listExamples() {\n    30\t  return fs.readdirSync(examplesDir)\n    31\t    // A file whose name starts with an underscore is a helper shared by examples, not an example.\n    32\t    .filter(file => /\\.(ts|tsx|html)$/.test(file) && !file.endsWith('.d.ts') && !file.startsWith('_'))\n    33\t    .sort()\n    34\t    .map(file => readExample(file));\n    35\t}\n    36\t\n    37\texport function readExample(file) {\n    38\t  const ext = path.extname(file).slice(1);\n    39\t  const name = path.basename(file, path.extname(file));\n    40\t  const source = fs.readFileSync(path.join(examplesDir, file), 'utf8');\n    41\t  const raises = RAISES.exec(source)?.[1].split(/, | and /) ?? [];\n    42\t  const targets = ext === 'ts' ? [...new Set([...source.matchAll(CHART_CALL)].map(m => m[2]))] : [];\n    43\t  if (ext === 'ts' && targets.length === 0) throw new Error(`${file}: no chart call with a '#id' target`);\n    44\t  return { file, name, ext, source, raises, noMarks: NO_MARKS.test(source), targets };\n    45\t}\n    46\t\n    47\t/**\n    48\t * The scripts of an .html example as JavaScript files, so `tsc` checks them against the package's\n    49\t * declarations like the .ts examples (with `checkJs`; see examples/tsconfig.html.json). A module script\n    50\t * imports 'axylo' itself; a classic script uses the `Axylo` global of the script-tag build, declared in\n    51\t * globals.d.ts from the same types.\n    52\t */\n    53\texport function htmlScripts(example) {\n    54\t  const out = [];\n    55\t  let n = 0;\n    56\t  for (const m of example.source.matchAll(MODULE_SCRIPT)) {\n    57\t    out.push({ file: `${example.name}.${++n}.js`, line: lineOf(example.source, m.index), code: m[1] });\n    58\t  }\n    59\t  for (const m of example.source.matchAll(CLASSIC_SCRIPT)) {\n    60\t    // `export {}` gives each classic script its own scope, as separate pages would.\n    61\t    out.push({ file: `${example.name}.${++n}.js`, line: lineOf(example.source, m.index), code: m[1] + '\\nexport {};\\n' });\n    62\t  }\n    63\t  return out;\n    64\t}\n    65\t\n    66\tfunction lineOf(text, index) {\n    67\t  return text.slice(0, index).split('\\n').length;\n    68\t}\n    69\t\n    70\t/** Writes the extracted scripts where apps/docs/examples/tsconfig.html.json includes them. */\n    71\texport function writeTypecheckInputs() {\n    72\t  const dir = path.join(cacheDir, 'html-scripts');\n    73\t  fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    74\t  fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\n    75\t  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, 'globals.d.ts'), \"declare const Axylo: typeof import('axylo');\\n\");\n    76\t  const map = {};\n    77\t  for (const example of listExamples().filter(e => e.ext === 'html')) {\n    78\t    for (const script of htmlScripts(example)) {\n    79\t      fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, script.file), script.code);\n    80\t      map[script.file] = { example: example.file, line: script.line };\n    81\t    }\n    82\t  }\n    83\t  return map;\n    84\t}\napps/docs/build.mjs\n     1\t// Builds the documentation site into apps/docs/dist. Needs the library built first (`npm run build`).\n     2\t// Usage: node apps/docs/build.mjs\n     3\timport { buildSite } from './lib/site.mjs';\n     4\t\n     5\tconst started = Date.now();\n     6\tconst result = await buildSite({ log: message => console.warn(message) });\n     7\tconst words = result.pages.reduce((sum, p) => sum + p.words, 0);\n     8\tconsole.log(`built ${result.pages.length} pages (${words} words), ${result.diagnostics} diagnostic pages and ${result.examples.length} examples in ${Date.now() - started} ms`);\n     9\tfor (const p of result.pages) console.log(`  ${p.page.padEnd(18)} ${String(p.words).padStart(5)} words`);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
