{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_116","type":"agent_message","text":"**The documentation site cannot currently be rebuilt from the shipped stylesheet.** The first-chart path can also produce a chart with no error diagnostics that shows the wrong calendar day, connects across a missing day, or changes an integer count. Of the 41 runnable examples, 36 passed strict type-checking and five failed.\n\nI reviewed the 19 authored pages, 29 generated diagnostic pages and 41 examples against the current checkout, including edits after `f9ed61b`. I created, edited and deleted no files. **Ran** below means I observed the result in Node. **Reasoned** means I traced the implementation or test assertions. Paths beginning with `pages/`, `examples/`, `lib/` or `test/` are relative to `apps/docs` unless otherwise identified. Library source paths are relative to `packages/axylo/src`.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **B · The build removes the previous site before encountering a reproducible failure.** `lib/site.mjs:50–65,98–106`, `pages/theming.md:9`. **Ran** the actual theme reader and asset-generation code with filesystem writes disabled. The light background came back as `light-dark(#ffffff, #16181d)`, then asset generation threw `axylo.css: no colour for --axylo-default-background (light)`. **Reasoned** from line 65 that an ordinary build would already have removed `outDir`. Read both explicit scheme selectors, validate the assets, and replace the old output only after the new site passes its checks. The stylesheet already provides both fixed palettes. [Build code](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/lib/site.mjs:50) · [Stylesheet](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:74)\n\n2. **B · The DX12 first-chart recipe introduces a field error of its own.** `pages/getting-started.md:31–53,74–89`, `data.md:47`, `options.md:57`, `line.md:23`, `area.md:22`, `bar.md:23`. **Ran** the five trap cases below. The troubleshooting snippet switches the npm example’s `month` and `visitors` to `day` and `sessions`, adds `series: 'channel'`, and drops the title. On ordinary single-series daily rows that extra field produces AX101. Omitting the name also produces AX140. A scalar `y` needs no `series`. Put a named, single-series daily example beside the first chart, use the same options for `validate`, and link directly to the numeric-string and missing-day fixes. [Public encoding](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/public.ts:70) · [Field checks](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/options.ts:253)\n\n   | DX12 fixture | What following the pages produced | Sentence the first-chart reader needs |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | UTC-midnight ISO dates | In Los Angeles, bare `x: 'day'` displayed February 24 UTC midnight as **February 23, 4:00 PM PST**, with AX111 and no error. Explicit `type: 'date'` displayed February 24 with no diagnostic. The correction is at `getting-started.md:78`, below the examples. | “For daily totals sent as UTC midnights, use `x: { field: 'day', type: 'date' }`.” |\n   | Numeric strings | Ordinary homogeneous decimal strings plotted in JavaScript with AX104. The inferred string field failed the bare-`y` TypeScript contract. The object form at `data.md:116` worked without the hint. | “For decimal strings, use `y: { field: 'sessions', parse: 'number' }` after checking the values fit your precision requirements.” |\n   | Unsorted rows | February 26, 24, 25 with values 3, 1, 2 read back as February 24→1, 25→2, 26→3, without diagnostics. `data.md:123` gives the right instruction. | “Pass dated rows in their original order. Axylo sorts by x and keeps each value with its row. Categories retain first-seen order.” |\n   | Missing days | February 24, 25, 27, 28 produced a February 26 gap and AX105. February 24 and 26 alone produced a connecting line and no diagnostic. | “When you know a day is missing, supply that day with `sessions: null`.” |\n   | Misspelled field | Nonempty untyped rows with `y: 'sesions'` produced AX101 and suggested `sessions`. Correcting the key cleared the error. Typed rows catch the typo at compile time. Empty data cannot establish which keys exist, and a suggestion requires a close match. | “On AX101, compare the field with the listed keys of a nonempty row. Use the suggested spelling when one is offered.” |\n\n3. **B · “Gaps … never a line drawn through them” promises more than the library can infer.** `pages/index.md:21`, `data.md:91–104`, `line.md:36`, `migrate-chartjs.md:51`, `data/diagnostics.mjs:84–86` (AX105). **Ran** the two missing-day cases above. Inference needs at least three observations in the series, intervals that are multiples of the smallest interval, and at least half the intervals equal to that smallest interval. Very sparse gaps are suppressed. Explicit `null` is the reliable instruction, including at the ends of a period. Explain that `missing: 'zero'` can fill inferred steps with zero and that a different series having an observation at an x does not by itself establish a missing value in this series. [Gap inference](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/steps.ts:74)\n\n4. **B · The numeric-string guidance can silently change database counts.** `pages/data.md:112–119`, `options.md:128–135`, `data/diagnostics.mjs:69–72,100–103` (AX104, AX106). **Ran** `'9007199254740993'` with `parse: 'number'`. The readout was **9,007,199,254,740,992**, with no diagnostic. `'1e999'` produced AX103. “A whole field … is unambiguous” conflates recognizing the syntax with preserving precision. Say that conversion uses JavaScript numbers, exponent notation is accepted, and exact integer counts need a safe-integer check before plotting. Also explain the field-wide rule. With a number or a nondecimal value mixed in, even otherwise valid decimal strings can be rejected. AX106 also covers non-string values such as booleans. [Value classification and conversion](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/values.ts:6)\n\n5. **B · Code following the event documentation can misinterpret dates and miss range changes.** `pages/updating.md:63,73–79`, `options.md:195–203`, `examples/zoom.html:21`, `examples/react-line.tsx:16` embedded at `pages/react.md:24`. **Ran** event and append probes. An instant is returned as a `Date`, a calendar day as `YYYY-MM-DD`, a wall time as offset-free ISO text, a category as its label, and a number as a number. A between-day zoom boundary can remain numeric to preserve the position. Pass the range directly to another chart’s `zoom()`. Converting wall time with `new Date()` can change its meaning. In the follow-latest case the window moved from `[2,3]` to `[3,4]` on append, but the only zoom event was `[2,3]`. Replace “Every change” with the user/API zoom operations that emit it. [Value conversion](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:226) · [Zoom dispatch](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:786)\n\n6. **B · The three headline KPIs disagree with the data plotted beneath them.** `examples/compact-tiles.html:10–21,29–35`, embedded at `pages/compact.md:9`. **Ran** the fixture arithmetic. The 30-day totals are **50,781 sessions** and **$184,909**, while the cards say 48,210 and $182,400. The latest daily error count and the 30-day daily mean are both 30, while the card says 37. Derive the headlines from `rows` and label the error statistic explicitly, for example “Errors on the latest day.” [Example](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/examples/compact-tiles.html:10)\n\n7. **B · The update demo labels the wrong week after two ordinary clicks.** `examples/update.html:32–44`, embedded at `pages/updating.md:39`. **Ran** the example’s own handlers in the order “Next week’s data”, “Add a subtitle”. The first row was `2026-03-09` and the subtitle was `Week of 2 March`. Use the current `start` in both handlers. [Example](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/examples/update.html:36)\n\n8. **B · The stack documentation invites readers to report a net total that the chart does not show.** `pages/area.md:7,34`, `bar.md:7,40–42,54`, `data.md:102`, `options.md:97`, `migrate-chartjs.md:23,50`, `data/diagnostics.mjs:158` (AX110). **Ran** the mixed-sign example. Q1 has **+165** above zero and **−60** below it. Its net is **+105**. Rename “Net revenue change” to “Revenue gains and losses”, or plot the computed net. Say the axis **includes** zero, the two edges represent separate sign totals, and the mixed-sign readout names both. For a missing stacked bar part the mark can be at the stack edge. The zero-baseline description applies to grouped bars. Incomplete stacks are also identified in the summary. [Stacked example](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/examples/bar-stacked.ts:12) · [Bar geometry](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:79) · [Stack readout](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/aligned.ts:110)\n\n9. **B · The donut limit counts positive arcs, not input categories.** `pages/donut.md:7,31–36`, `examples/donut-many.ts:3`, `data/diagnostics.mjs:216–219` (AX121). **Ran** eight positive values plus zero and null. There was no grouping. Nine positive values plus zero and null produced **Other (2)**, with zero and null still listed individually. State that the seven largest positive slices stay separate once the positive count exceeds eight, the table retains every original category, and shares have at most one fraction digit. [Spec F8](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/02-product-spec.md:101) · [Share formatter](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/format/number.ts:122)\n\n10. **B · Display names, series keys and source-row identities are treated as interchangeable.** `pages/data.md:16,45,133,148`, `options.md:38,135,202–206`, `theming.md:17–26`, `updating.md:79`. **Ran** a wide series with field `a` and label `Direct`. `point.series` was `a`. Use the wide field key in `colors` and event handlers, and the label for display. A long series uses the grouping field’s value. Generated donut “Other” has a distinct key and muted paint. An inferred position or grouped item can have `row: null` and `index: -1`. Show a null check before using an event to look up a source record. [Colour binding](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:898) · [Point construction](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1482)\n\n11. **B · An invisible compact reference can flatten the entire sparkline.** `pages/compact.md:23–27`, `options.md:81–83`, `line.md:43`, `bar.md:46`, `scatter.md:41`. **Ran** a compact line with values 2–4 and a reference at 1,000. Its y domain became `[0,1000]`, and the reference entered the summary. Replace “have no effect” with “compact charts hide reference marks, but references still affect automatic domains and the description.” On full charts, author bounds can exclude a reference. A horizontal bar chart also swaps the screen directions of x and y references. [Domain calculation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:258) · [Reader description](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/reader/index.ts:221)\n\n12. **B · The ownership and update-cost promises are too strong for large datasets.** `pages/data.md:146–150`, `examples/data-columns.ts:3`, `pages/updating.md:43–55`, `migrate-chartjs.md:37,59,69`, `migrate-recharts.md:33`, `react.md:28–31`, `data/diagnostics.mjs:383–386` (AX151). **Ran** typed-column identity checks. A finite sorted aligned y column was borrowed. Unsorted positions or an inserted gap caused allocation with the same finite values. Grouping, scatter filtering and type conversion can require new storage too. Keep the instruction to replace input arrays on update. Describe borrowing and incremental append as conditional optimizations. Out-of-order append can rebuild and strict mode rejects its warning. Resume shows the rows retained under `keep`. For React, “the same content” is a heuristic comparing length and endpoints, and comparing an option object by content entails work even when no chart update follows. [Normalization](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/normalize.ts:255) · [Append fallback](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store.ts:929) · [React heuristic](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/react/src/index.ts:112)\n\n13. **B · The documented x-kind vote predicts the wrong axis.** `pages/data.md:75–83`, `data/diagnostics.mjs:114–117` (AX107). **Ran** three categorical strings, two dates and two numbers. “Takes the kind most of them have” predicts category. The chart selected date, retained the two dates and reported AX107. Category wins if its count is at least the **combined** recognized count. Otherwise the largest recognized kind wins, with a fixed tie order. Recommend an explicit x type for heterogeneous feeds. AX107 also covers unusable numeric x, series or donut labels, and invalid domains or references, where the option can be ignored without dropping a data row. [Vote](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/x.ts:122) · [Reference validation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/references.ts:24)\n\n14. **B · The diagnostic severity is insufficient to predict what remains on screen or whether a call throws.** `pages/options.md:20`, `diagnostics.md:25–29,53`, `data.md:127`, `line.md:42`, `scatter.md:23`, `data/diagnostics.mjs:128–132,368–372,428–433`, `lib/site.mjs:413–416` (AX108, AX150, AX199). **Ran** the series and scatter cases. Duplicate x can suppress one series while peers still draw. With no drawable series the chart shows an error state and retains an inspectable table where available. A scatter y **list** can produce warning AX150 and an error state. The generic “option is ignored” outcome is wrong there. **Reasoned** from strict delivery that a presentation-stage AX199 does not throw from the original call. Its underlying exception can go to `console.error`, while the diagnostic follows diagnostic delivery. Generate severity text separately from the specific effect and phase. [Error-state selection](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:924) · [Delivery](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/delivery.ts:65)\n\n15. **B · The chart-type “Limit” rows conflate rows, marks and available visual distinctions.** `pages/scatter.md:7,38–40`, `line.md:41`, `area.md:40`, `bar.md:44–45`, `compact.md:21`, `index.md:18`, `data/diagnostics.mjs:230–233,246–249,261–264,277–280` (AX130–133). **Ran** scatter with valid x and unplottable y. It had no point but did have an in-range table row reading **No data**. AX133 concerns more than 50,000 plottable points. The view draws visible points without simplification. **Reasoned** from the cue and geometry code that eight is a warning threshold. Bars use fill patterns, including in multiseries compact mode, with 32 distinct default combinations before repetition. AX132 compares visible x slots with CSS pixels. It does not establish that every grouped bar is thinner than one pixel. [Scatter normalization](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/normalize.ts:348) · [Table](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/reader/table.ts:121) · [Bar widths and patterns](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:74) · [Spec F9](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/02-product-spec.md:102)\n\n16. **B · The interaction instructions describe the previous tooltip and an obsolete release status.** `pages/index.md:16,43`, `getting-started.md:63`, `line.md:36–38`, `area.md:34`, `bar.md:37`, `accessibility.md:13,62`, `migrate-chartjs.md:54`. **Reasoned** from revised decision 0004 and the implementation. Line and area pick by x, bars by band, scatter within 24 CSS px, and donut by arc. The readout is anchored to the datum. Hovered text passes pointer events through. Click or tap pins it and enables row selection. Escape dismisses it until a different datum is reached, before a further Escape leaves single-series reading. The tooltip shows up to eight rows, fewer if necessary, with an overflow count. A small plot uses a reserved two-line strip when enough plot height remains. Remove the “being finished” list. Pan buttons and the table overlay exist, and **no chart type zooms a category axis**. [Decision 0004](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/decisions/0004-tooltip-and-focused-text.md:12) · [Strip sizing](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1225) · [Zoom guard](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:762)\n\n17. **B · The accessibility claims exceed the evidence allowed by §3.8.** `pages/index.md:3`, `compact.md:3`, `accessibility.md:3,11–17,54–64`, `updating.md:49`, `migrate-chartjs.md:33,64`. **Reasoned** from the evidence record and focused-text implementation. Replace “works with … a screen reader”, “can rely on”, and unconditional claims about what is spoken with observable behavior. The chart exposes a name, summary, focused value text and polite state updates. Appending alone need not rewrite a focused value just because its ordinal changed, but a changed or evicted focused datum can update it. Speech depends on the reader. State the limits alongside the claims: automated structure checks, developer rehearsal planned, no screen reader run in the cited evidence, no usability testing with disabled users, and Firefox, Safari and phones unverified. The recorded browser evidence is desktop Chrome. [Spec §3.8](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/02-product-spec.md:214) · [Focused-text decision](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/decisions/0004-tooltip-and-focused-text.md)\n\n18. **M · The keyboard map sends readers looking for controls that may be absent.** `pages/accessibility.md:12,19,29,37`, `getting-started.md:61–62`, `index.md:17`, `options.md:35`. **Reasoned.** Say “up to two tab stops with the table closed”. Compact charts have none, and the toolbar depends on available controls. Donut legend buttons select slices, including a single slice, and do not carry the series-toggle pressed state. Pager and Jump appear only above 100 table rows. Replace “A larger step” with “Page Up moves forward and Page Down backward by one tenth of the point count, rounded down, with a minimum of one.” [Interaction map](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:137) · [Page distance](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/search.ts:19) · [Table pager](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:137)\n\n19. **M · Markdown escaping leaves unsafe link destinations intact.** `lib/markdown.mjs:203–211`, `lib/site.mjs:232–234,476–479`. **Ran** the harmless input `[Custom](custom:chapter)`. It emitted `<a href=\"custom:chapter\">Custom</a>`. **Reasoned** that the same unrestricted scheme handling permits active URL schemes, which the checker skips. Raw text escaping works in this example. The missing check is on navigation. Allow site-relative links, fragments and the intended external schemes, and reject other schemes before emitting `href`. [Converter](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/lib/markdown.mjs:203)\n\n20. **M · Link and include checks can approve material that will be missing or wrong on the published site.** `lib/site.mjs:239–247,251–264,274–293,458–483`, `lib/markdown.mjs:131–148`. **Ran** the checker on the existing output. It returned zero broken links, although the 19 top-level HTML pages contained **58 references to 55 distinct `../…` destinations**. The checker can satisfy these from the checkout. **Reasoned** that serving `dist/` alone loses source files and decision records or resolves them to different resources. Publish the linked files or use revision-pinned repository links, then check against the deployment root. Validate `[table: …]` targets, which are currently ignored. Restrict source includes to intended canonical paths and fail on missing required snippets. Two adjacent directive lines also become one ordinary paragraph unless separated by a blank line. Treat each directive as a block. [Include implementation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/lib/site.mjs:244) · [Link checker](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/lib/site.mjs:458)\n\n21. **M · Five HTML examples fail the advertised standard of strict package checking.** `examples/tsconfig.html.json:5–8`, `test/examples.browser.test.ts:57–63`, `examples/node/tsconfig.json:3`, `pages/diagnostics.md:61–69`. **Ran** strict no-emit checks against the declarations, with library checking enabled. The 24 TS and five TSX entries passed. Of 12 HTML entries, seven passed and five produced 13 nullable-DOM errors, listed below. The documentation config turns off `strictNullChecks`. Narrow the element types in the examples and enable it. Separately, the Node examples’ ES-only config passes with skipped declaration checking but reports `Cannot find name 'HTMLElement'` when checking the package declaration. Document the DOM **type-library** requirement for that configuration. The npm and React NodeNext consumer fixtures both passed with DOM types and declaration checking enabled. [HTML config](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/examples/tsconfig.html.json:5) · [Public target type](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/public.ts:158)\n\n22. **M · Readers cannot reproduce several otherwise valid examples from the displayed source.** `pages/getting-started.md:31–51`, `migrate-chartjs.md:15,25,35`, `migrate-recharts.md:15,25,35`, `lib/examples.mjs:23–43`, `lib/site.mjs:179–199`. **Ran** all entries with their required hosts supplied, and **reasoned** through what the site adds. “Each of these is complete” omits the npm mount element and React mounting step. The live first chart uses 90 daily channel rows, different from the four monthly visitor rows in the installation snippets. The wrapper synthesizes TS target elements, a React root and an import map. Six migrations import `_phase1-data.ts`, which the displayed example does not supply. Show the required host next to each snippet, make the shared fixture available with the example, identify the module-resolution prerequisite, and run the actual introductory fixture beside its source. [Wrapper](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/lib/site.mjs:179) · [Missing-target behavior](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:219)\n\n23. **M · The examples test does not prove DX10 or the chart’s meaning.** `test/examples.browser.test.ts:45–63,87–122`, `lib/site.mjs:119–168`. **Reasoned mutation:** change the Direct base in `examples/first-chart.ts:8` from `31000` to `3100`. The chart still has a name, nonempty marks and the same diagnostics, so the assertions would pass once the build runs. The test also accepts any positive chart count, checks a state message without checking absence of marks, and waits three frames without driving the documented controls. It loads workspace `dist` and an import map. That leaves tarball contents, export conditions, declarations and dependency resolution in a clean consumer unproven for the 41 examples. Compile and render these entries from installed packed artifacts, and assert representative values, expected chart counts and the interactions each example teaches. The separate packed first-chart fixtures cover a smaller set. [Example assertions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/test/examples.browser.test.ts:102) · [DX10](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/02-product-spec.md:231)\n\n24. **M · The three coverage tests can pass after their principal user-facing facts become false.** **Reasoned** the following mutations against the actual assertions. None requires changing the example input.\n\n   | Test and location | Mutation | Would the test catch it? |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | `test/options.test.ts:96–106,120–125` | Change the tooltip type to `string` and its default to `false`, retaining the key. | **No.** Only first-column keys are extracted. Check declared types and executable defaults separately. |\n   | `test/theming.test.ts:27–37` | Swap the documented private defaults of `--axylo-axis` and `--axylo-grid`. | **No additional failure.** Both names exist and both remain covered. The current hex-parser failure is independent. Assert each public token’s actual fallback binding in both schemes. |\n   | `test/diagnostics.test.ts:28–42`, `test/diagnostics.browser.test.ts:39` | Replace AX107’s cause with “duplicate x”, retaining its input and level. | **No.** The prose remains nonempty and the fixture still emits AX107. Assert the fixture’s field, effect and reader-visible outcome, and review the causal sentence against that fixture. |\n\n25. **M · Several generated diagnostic pages prescribe the wrong remedy or describe the wrong effect.** `pages/diagnostics.md:17,25–29,53,71`, `getting-started.md:68`, `index.md:23`, `options.md:217–219`, `bar.md:43`, `data/diagnostics.mjs` at the lines below. **Reasoned** against the registry and call sites. `field`, `rows` and `count` are optional. Some hints materially affect the plot, including AX105. Node can check a missing name but cannot resolve a DOM id or measure a plot. Correct these individual entries:\n\n   | Page and source line | Corrected scope |\n   |---|---|\n   | AX100 `:13`, AX101 `:27` | Invalid column lengths or shapes also fail the column check. Field-presence checking needs evidence from the data. A spelling suggestion is conditional. |\n   | AX102 `:41`, AX103 `:55` | An absent y can become zero under the declared policy. An absent x or series can drop a row. Non-finite domain/reference inputs can cause an option to be ignored. `NaN` in a floating typed value column is ordinary missing data. |\n   | AX111 `:170`, AX140 `:306` | AX111 needs distinct instants and displays the configured zone. A missing `labelledBy` element falls back to a supplied title without AX140. |\n   | AX142 `:335`, AX143 `:352` | The small-chart summary can occupy two lines. The table control requires an enabled table. The horizontal-bars suggestion applies to vertical categorical bars. Supply the chart type and x kind in the registry sample if the displayed message promises that suggestion. |\n   | AX152 `:399`, AX160 `:413` | A bad zone can be diagnosed even when the axis does not display instants. Invalid `Intl` options, such as currency style without a currency, can cause AX160 without a throwing callback. A null slot does not require a user value formatter to handle `null`. |\n\n   [Registry](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/diagnostics/registry.ts:43) · [Column checks](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/options.ts:129) · [Formatter and naming stages](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1042) · [Small-chart CSS](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:146)\n\n26. **M · Platform, CSP and theme claims mix targets, evidence and implementation details.** `pages/getting-started.md:25`, `stability.md:21,29–36`, `theming.md:13,38,46,54–59`, `data/diagnostics.mjs:319–323` (AX141). **Reasoned** against the source, recorded tests and decisions. Styles may be adopted, supplied by standalone CSS, or installed through a fallback `<style>`. Packed Chromium CSP tests exist. The macOS/iOS qualifier in the support matrix belongs to Safari. Keep browser targets separate from verified environments. React declarations also live in the React package. Theme observation covers specified media and ancestor attribute changes. AX141 skips contrast judgment when the backdrop cannot be resolved. SVG is decision 0002’s provisional working default. Remove the assertion about exactly how the toolbar prints. Describe decision 0003’s refitted palette measurements per matching scheme, simulated vision and tested fill opacity. [Style installation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/styles.ts:29) · [CSP tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/csp.browser.test.ts) · [Support targets](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/02-product-spec.md:80) · [Palette measurements](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/decisions/0003-default-palette.md:65)\n\n27. **M · The migration pages turn fixture choices into requirements of competing libraries.** `pages/migrate-chartjs.md:5–23,37–65`, `migrate-recharts.md:5–23,33,43–66`. **Ran** the installed Chart.js linear parser and the numeric scale used by Recharts with `'40'`. Both produced 40. **Reasoned** the remaining claims from the local evidence below. Replace “least configuration” with “configuration used in this comparison.” On the Axylo side, the target is a selector or `HTMLElement`, typed columns are an optional input, and a visible title and a date-axis title need author input. Dense lines can retain end, interval and isolated markers. [Public target](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/public.ts:158) · [Line markers](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/lines.ts:21)\n\n   | Migration claim | What can be verified here |\n   |---|---|\n   | Chart.js versions, quoted configurations, adapter and time scale, parallel arrays, sizing options, bars without a target, array mutation and `update()`, tuned parsing/decimation/animation/markers | **Harness and installed packages.** These are supported choices. The tuned configuration also demonstrates a different data shape. The adapter and timezone determine how instants are formatted. [Chart.js harness](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/research/harness/src/libs/chartjs.js) · [Tuned harness](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/research/harness/src/libs/chartjs-tuned.js) |\n   | Chart.js table of options, mixed line dataset, canvas, events, lifecycle, gap handling, chart types and numeric coercion | **Installed Chart.js and harness.** Qualify rotation as the observed result for the comparison’s width. The annotation plugin is absent locally. Its exact API, the