. **Ran** the default tick formatter at 50,000 and got `50,000`, where the page gives `50K`. Compact defaults begin at a largest tick of one million, with scientific notation for extreme scales. **Reasoned** from the public types that `XValue` should be defined on first use as `number | string | Date`, and `{ columns }` should say one equal-length `ArrayLike` per field. In a wide chart the first y field supplies the shared domain. Replace “Every built-in string” with “reader-facing messages”. Developer diagnostics have fixed registry wording. Give a translated note retaining `{seeTable}`, which the reader can remove with the table disabled. The generated defaults pick up `panLeft`, `panRight`, `jumpNotFound`, `plotInstructions`, `seeTable`, `totalMixed`, `incompleteAt` and `incompleteCount` on a successful rebuild. Also change “Take seven numbers” to “four days, two readings per day.” [Tick formatting](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/format/number.ts:200) · [Shared domain](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/stages.ts:91) · [Conditional table text](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/reader/index.ts:49)\n\n29. **M · The build can combine artifacts from different revisions or environments.** `build.mjs:1–6`, `lib/site.mjs:24–42,74–78,138–146,370–382`. **Ran** development and production React export enumeration. The lists differ, including `captureOwnerStack` and `act`. Wrapper generation reads ambient `require()` exports while esbuild explicitly produces development code. **Reasoned** that the existence-only library check can also combine stale bundles/CSS with current source messages, registry and package version. Generate wrappers under the same explicit condition as the bundle, and build or verify all inputs from the same revision. A deterministic example order does not resolve either mismatch. [Vendor build](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/lib/site.mjs:131)\n\n30. **m · Valid-looking links and headings produce broken navigation.** `lib/markdown.mjs:51–52,78–87,206–210`, `lib/site.mjs:470–483`. **Ran** `[Guide](guide(v2).md)`. The emitted destination was `guide(v2`, followed by literal `.md)`. Headings `Notes`, `Notes`, `Notes-2`, followed by a blockquoted heading `Notes`, produced IDs `notes`, `notes-2`, `notes-2`, `notes`. Parse balanced destinations, reserve emitted IDs across the whole page including quotes, and reject duplicate IDs during the build. Validate local `#L…` fragments on site HTML instead of exempting all of them. [Inline parser](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/lib/markdown.mjs:203) · [Anchor checker](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/apps/docs/lib/site.mjs:470)\n\n## Example-by-example result\n\nI bundled all 41 entries with esbuild in memory and exercised their **50 initial chart configurations** through validation and the library’s recording controller host at 752 CSS px in `America/Los_Angeles`, with fixed text metrics. The initial models produced the declared diagnostic sets. This verifies data and model behavior. Browser painting, physical pointer/keyboard interaction, timer progression and React hydration were outside this run.\n\nEach name below is one entry. **Pass** means strict compilation against the package declarations, including strict null checks for extracted HTML scripts. For adaptation, TS entries need matching mount elements, TSX entries need a React root, and the 11 module-HTML entries need a bundler or import map. The script-tag entry needs the IIFE at its stated path.\n\n| Examples | Strict result | Fit to the page and adaptation |\n|---|---|---|\n| `first-chart`, `script-tag` | Pass both | Both construct a first chart. The live daily fixture differs from the introductory monthly fixture. Copying the script-tag page also requires copying or locating `axylo.iife.js`. |\n| `data-long`, `data-wide`, `data-columns` | Pass all three | Comparable four-day, two-channel data. The rows are adaptable. The typed-column borrowing comment needs finding 12. |\n| `dates`, `numeric-strings`, `unsorted`, `missing` | Pass all four | Demonstrate the intended contrast, declared string conversion, ordering and inferable gap respectively. `dates` uses a different date representation for the correction. `missing` has enough observations to infer cadence. Neither example establishes the broader promises in findings 2–4. |\n| `line-time`, `line-dirty` | Pass both | Time trend and deliberate invalid-data disclosures match their uses. `line-dirty` uses a type assertion to admit the deliberately malformed fixture. Do not copy that assertion as input validation. |\n| `area-stacked`, `area-incomplete` | Pass both | Demonstrate ordinary stacking and an incomplete stack. Neither demonstrates a mixed-sign area readout. |\n| `bar-target`, `bar-horizontal`, `bar-stacked` | Pass all three | Target and horizontal grouping fit the prose. The mixed-sign fixture works, but its title claims a net value the marks do not encode. |\n| `scatter-basic`, `scatter-ties` | Pass both | Show two measures and coincident valid points. Neither demonstrates the retained table row for missing y. |\n| `donut-basic`, `donut-many` | Pass both | Adaptable part-to-whole data. The latter’s comment miscounts which categories go into Other. |\n| `compact-tiles`, `compact-dirty` | Pass both | The dirty-data example supplies its own tile and demonstrates the disclosure. The three-card example’s headlines disagree with its source rows. |\n| `a11y-card`, `states`, `units` | Pass all three | Show author-supplied naming/context, four state panels, and ratio/unit formatting. `units` explicitly requests compact ticks in one panel, so it cannot establish the claimed default. |\n| `theme-colors`, `theme-tokens` | Pass both | Show long-series colour mapping and CSS token overrides. Neither exercises a wide field key different from its display label. |\n| `theme-toggle` | **Fail**, one DOM nullability error | The theme-switch setup fits the prose. Narrow the button lookup before attaching its listener. |\n| `diagnostics-listener`, `strict` | **Fail**, one and two DOM nullability errors respectively | The listener and rejected-update examples fit their purpose. Their element lookups require narrowing. |\n| `stream`, `react-stream` | Pass both | Show the initial rows and append setup. Live progression and pause/resume were not exercised by the initial-model check. The React example needs its root. |\n| `react-line` | Pass | The event example works for its own date-only fixture. Its epoch-milliseconds comment teaches the wrong general rule. |\n| `update`, `zoom` | **Fail**, five and four DOM nullability errors respectively | `update` also gives the wrong subtitle in the tested click sequence. `zoom` uses obsolete event-conversion advice. |\n| `migrate-trend`, `migrate-target`, `migrate-stream` | Pass all three | Use the comparison’s trend, target and stream fixtures. Each needs the shared `_phase1-data.ts` in addition to its mount element. |\n| `recharts-trend`, `recharts-target`, `recharts-stream` | Pass all three | Same fixture dependency plus a React root. The trend example explicitly supplies text the page says requires no code. |\n\n**Claims without a matching runnable demonstration.** The line/area pages lack a dense-line example exposing simplification versus full-resolution lookup. The chart-type pages lack an over-eight Cartesian series example, a mixed-sign area, and scatter table retention for missing y. Updating lacks event round-tripping between charts, strict out-of-order append and follow-latest event behavior. Accessibility/options lack a translated `{seeTable}` example with the table disabled. Theming lacks a forced-colours or print demonstration. The React page’s Suspense lifecycle claim is not exercised by either displayed React example. The diagnostic pages’ minimal inputs and the separate library tests serve different purposes from these reader-facing examples.\n\n## Verification and limits\n\nThe documentation Node suite ran with caches disabled. Its options test normally creates two compiler-probe files. To respect read-only operation, I checked that the existing files were byte-identical to what the test would write and suppressed those two writes. The failure was the theme-default assertion in finding 1. The last result lines were:\n\n```text\nTest Files  1 failed | 3 passed (4)\n     Tests  1 failed | 134 passed (135)\n```\n\nI also ran the strict compiler checks, Node validation and server-render checks, and the two NodeNext consumer configurations. I did not launch a browser, run a destructive site build, install a packed distribution, or conduct a clean-room DX12 agent rehearsal. Deployment-link findings assume the published artifact is `apps/docs/dist` alone. No contract change is needed for the documentation corrections.\n\n## Page accounting\n\nCounts refer to numbered findings against page content or its embedded examples. A build or test defect is counted against a page only where the finding identifies a specific page claim.\n\n```text\naccessibility.md       4  (#16, #17, #18, #28)\narea.md                4  (#2, #8, #15, #16)\nbar.md                 6  (#2, #8, #11, #15, #16, #25)\ncompact.md             4  (#6, #11, #15, #17)\nconformance.md         accurate as written\ndata.md                9  (#2, #3, #4, #8, #10, #12, #13, #14, #28)\ndiagnostics.md         3  (#14, #21, #25)\ndonut.md               1  (#9)\ngetting-started.md     6  (#2, #16, #18, #22, #25, #26)\nindex.md               6  (#3, #15, #16, #17, #18, #25)\nline.md                6  (#2, #3, #11, #14, #15, #16)\nmigrate-chartjs.md     7  (#3, #8, #12, #16, #17, #22, #27)\nmigrate-recharts.md    3  (#12, #22, #27)\noptions.md            10  (#2, #4, #5, #8, #10, #11, #14, #18, #25, #28)\nreact.md               2  (#5, #12)\nscatter.md             3  (#11, #14, #15)\nstability.md           2  (#26, #28)\ntheming.md             3  (#1, #10, #26)\nupdating.md            5  (#5, #7, #10, #12, #